window.QUESTIONS=[{"c": "tech", "s": "過去問 令和3年10月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_musen_0310/", "k": "13", "al": [], "q": "図に示す電気回路の抵抗 𝑅 の値の大きさを 3 倍にすると、𝑅 によって消費される電力は、何倍になるか。", "x": "<div>\n    <img loading=\"lazy\" \n      src=\"img/0ecf525ce8.png\" \n      alt=\"3陸特_無線工学(令和3年10月)_問題13\"  >\n  </div>", "o": ["1/9倍", "1/3倍", "3倍", "9倍"], "a": 1, "e": "<p><b>\n      直流電源と抵抗だけの単純な直列回路では、消費電力𝑃は以下の式で表せます：\n      </b></p>\n\n      <p>\\( P = \\frac{V^2}{R} \\)</p>\n\n      <p><b>\n      抵抗𝑅を3倍にすると…<br>\n      新しい抵抗：3𝑅<br>\n      新しい電力：\n      </b></p>\n\n      <p>\\( P' = \\frac{V^2}{3R} = \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{V^2}{R} = \\frac{1}{3}P \\)</p>", "ee": "In a simple series circuit of a DC source and a resistor, the power consumed is: \\( P = \\frac{V^2}{R} \\)<br>If R is tripled, the new resistance is 3R and the new power is: \\( P' = \\frac{V^2}{3R} = \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{V^2}{R} = \\frac{1}{3}P \\)", "eg": false, "eq": "If the value of resistance R in the circuit shown is tripled, by what factor does the power consumed by R change?", "eo": ["1/9 times", "1/3 times", "3 times", "9 times"], "v": [0, 362, 2, 5, 6, 330, 368, 327, 329, 367]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "過去問 令和3年10月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_musen_0310/", "k": "14", "al": [], "q": "次の記述の(　　　)内に入れるべき字句の組合せで、正しいのはどれか。<br>\n  半導体は、周囲の温度が上昇するとその電気抵抗が ( A ) し、内部を流れる電流は ( B ) する。", "x": "", "o": ["(A) 増加 (B) 減少", "(A) 増加 (B) 増加", "(A) 減少 (B) 増加", "(A) 減少 (B) 減少"], "a": 2, "e": "<b>半導体の温度特性について：<br>\n      半導体（例：シリコンやゲルマニウム）は、温度が上がるとキャリア（電子や正孔）の数が増加します。<br>\n      その結果、電気を流しやすくなり、抵抗値は下がります（＝A：減少）<br>\n      抵抗が小さくなると、同じ電圧でも、より多くの電流が流れる（＝B：増加）ことになります。<br>\n      <br>\n      純粋な抵抗の場合は、温度上昇により、金属中の自由電子が振動し抵抗値が上がり、電流値が下がります。<br>\n      特性が反対になりますので注意が必要です。<br>\n      </b>\n\n      <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/9ab211b6b1.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No3_解答14\"  >\n      </div>", "ee": "Temperature behavior of semiconductors: when the temperature of a semiconductor (e.g. silicon or germanium) rises, the number of carriers (electrons and holes) increases. It conducts more easily, so its resistance goes down (A: decreases). With lower resistance, more current flows at the same voltage (B: increases).<br>For an ordinary metal resistor it is the opposite: heat makes the free electrons vibrate more, so resistance rises and current falls. Don't mix the two up. <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/9ab211b6b1.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No3_解答14\"  >\n      </div>", "eg": false, "eq": "Which combination of words correctly fills the blanks? When the surrounding temperature of a semiconductor rises, its electrical resistance (A), and the current flowing through it (B).", "eo": ["(A) increases (B) decreases", "(A) increases (B) increases", "(A) decreases (B) increases", "(A) decreases (B) decreases"], "v": [15, 315, 322, 339, 411, 2, 8, 16, 17, 18, 19, 305, 316, 383, 426, 427, 304, 314]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "過去問 令和3年10月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_musen_0310/", "k": "15", "al": [], "q": "図は、三素子八木・宇田アンテナ（八木アンテナ）の構成を示したものである。各素子の名称の組合せで、正しいのはどれか。ただし、A、B、C の長さは、A ＜ B ＜ C の関係があるものとする。", "x": "<div>\n    <img loading=\"lazy\" \n      src=\"img/66be29032a.png\" \n      alt=\"八木アンテナ\"  >\n  </div>", "o": ["A:導波器 B:放射器 C:反射器", "A:導波器 B:反射器 C:放射器", "A:反射器 B:放射器 C:導波器", "A:反射器 B:導波器 C:放射器"], "a": 0, "e": "", "ee": "In a Yagi antenna the three elements have different lengths: the director (導波器) is the shortest and sits at the front, the radiator (放射器) is about λ/2 and is fed with the signal, and the reflector (反射器) is the longest and sits at the back. With A &lt; B &lt; C: A = director, B = radiator, C = reflector.", "eg": true, "eq": "The figure shows the structure of a three-element Yagi-Uda antenna (Yagi antenna). Which combination of element names is correct? Assume the lengths satisfy A < B < C.", "eo": ["A: director, B: radiator, C: reflector", "A: director, B: reflector, C: radiator", "A: reflector, B: radiator, C: director", "A: reflector, B: director, C: radiator"], "v": [23, 24, 25, 322, 339, 20, 21, 22, 330, 384, 385, 386, 430, 329, 428, 429]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "過去問 令和3年10月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_musen_0310/", "k": "16", "al": [{"s": "例題集 No.3", "k": "16", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no3/"}], "q": "超短波（VHF）帯では、一般にアンテナの高さを高くした方が電波の到達距離が延びるのはなぜか。", "x": "", "o": ["見通し距離が延びるから。", "地表波の減衰が少なくなるから。", "対流圏散乱波が伝わりやすくなるから。", "スポラジックE層（Es層）の反射によって伝わりやすくなるから。"], "a": 0, "e": "", "ee": "VHF waves travel mostly in straight lines (direct waves) and are not reflected back by the ionosphere. Their range is limited by the horizon, so raising the antenna extends the line-of-sight distance and the waves reach farther.", "eg": true, "eq": "In the VHF band, why does raising the antenna height generally extend the distance radio waves can reach?", "eo": ["Because the line-of-sight distance becomes longer.", "Because the attenuation of the ground wave decreases.", "Because tropospheric scatter waves propagate more easily.", "Because waves propagate more easily via reflection from the sporadic E layer (Es layer)."], "v": [31, 30, 28, 32, 34, 35, 387, 33, 36, 138, 335, 350, 352, 355, 372, 373, 388, 412]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "過去問 令和3年10月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_musen_0310/", "k": "18", "al": [], "q": "アナログ方式の回路計（テスタ）のゼロオーム調整つまみは、何を測定するときに必要となるか。", "x": "", "o": ["静電容量", "抵抗", "電流", "電圧"], "a": 1, "e": "<b>アナログテスタで抵抗を測る前の基本手順は以下の通り：<br>\n      測定レンジを選ぶ（適切なΩレンジに切り替える）<br>\n      テストリード（テスト棒）を短絡（接触）する<br>\n      ゼロオーム調整（0Ω校正）をする<br>\n      <br>\n      最初にレンジを選ばないと、調整する基準が変わってしまう<br>\n      ゼロオーム調整は、テストリードを短絡して行う必要がある<br></b>", "ee": "Basic steps before measuring resistance with an analog tester:<br>1. Select the measurement range (switch to a suitable Ω range).<br>2. Short the test leads together.<br>3. Do the zero-ohm (0 Ω) adjustment.<br>If you don't select the range first, the reference you adjusted to changes. The zero-ohm adjustment must be done with the test leads shorted.", "eg": false, "eq": "On an analog circuit tester, the zero-ohm adjustment knob is needed when measuring what?", "eo": ["Capacitance", "Resistance", "Current", "Voltage"], "v": [10, 59, 2, 7, 8, 61, 63, 331, 371, 476]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "過去問 令和3年10月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_musen_0310/", "k": "19", "al": [], "q": "振幅変調（A3E）波と比べたときの周波数変調（F3E）波の占有周波数帯幅の一般的な特徴は、次のうちどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["同じ", "広い", "狭い", "半分"], "a": 1, "e": "<b>FMは高音質・ノイズ耐性に優れる一方、広い周波数帯域を必要とするのが特徴です。</b>", "ee": "FM offers high audio quality and good noise resistance, but it needs a wide frequency bandwidth.", "eg": false, "eq": "Compared with an amplitude-modulated (A3E) wave, what is the general characteristic of the occupied bandwidth of a frequency-modulated (F3E) wave?", "eo": ["The same", "Wider", "Narrower", "Half"], "v": [72, 67, 66, 334, 332, 340, 374, 413, 414, 432, 304, 390]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "過去問 令和3年10月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_musen_0310/", "k": "21", "al": [], "q": "次の記述は、デジタル変調について述べたものである。(　　　)内に入れるべき字句は次のうちどれか。<br>\n    <br>\n    FSKは、ベースバンド信号に応じて搬送波の周波数を切り替える方式である。また、4値FSKは、1回の変調（シンボル）で(　　　)ビットの情報を伝送できる。", "x": "", "o": ["2", "3", "4", "5"], "a": 0, "e": "<b>4値（4段階）のFSKでは、1シンボルあたり2ビットの情報を伝送できます。</b>", "ee": "4-level FSK carries 2 bits of information per symbol (4 = 2²).", "eg": false, "eq": "The following describes digital modulation. Which word fills the blank? FSK switches the carrier frequency according to the baseband signal. 4-level FSK can transmit ( ) bits of information per modulation (symbol).", "eo": [null, null, null, null], "v": [433, 42, 73, 315, 65, 81, 82, 305, 316, 321, 331, 336, 415, 304, 314, 327, 416]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "過去問 令和3年10月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_musen_0310/", "k": "22", "al": [], "q": "図は、デジタル無線受信装置の概念図例を示したものである。 (　　　)内に入れるべき字句を下の番号から選べ。", "x": "<div>\n    <img loading=\"lazy\" \n      src=\"img/dc1ec81dd9.png\" \n      alt=\"無線工学No2_問題22\"  >\n  </div>", "o": ["周波数変換器", "IDC回路", "AFC回路", "D/A変換器"], "a": 3, "e": "<b>図の中で、受信機から出力されたデジタル信号が、スピーカで音声として再生される前に「アナログ信号」に変換されています。<br>\n      この変換（デジタル → アナログ）を行う装置をD/A変換器（Digital to Analog Converter）といいます。</b>\n      <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/aefd2229fe.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No2_解答22\"  >\n      </div>", "ee": "In the diagram, the digital signal from the receiver is converted to an analog signal before the speaker plays it as sound. The device that does this digital → analog conversion is a D/A converter (Digital-to-Analog Converter). <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/aefd2229fe.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No2_解答22\"  >\n      </div>", "eg": false, "eq": "The figure is an example conceptual diagram of a digital radio receiver. Choose the item that fills the blank.", "eo": ["Frequency converter", "IDC circuit (instantaneous deviation control)", "AFC circuit (automatic frequency control)", "D/A converter"], "v": [96, 92, 94, 95, 315, 1, 306, 316, 319, 330, 391, 314, 317, 329, 417]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "過去問 令和3年10月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_musen_0310/", "k": "23", "al": [], "q": "スーパヘテロダイン受信機の周波数変換部の働きは、次のうちどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["受信周波数を中間周波数に変える。", "中間周波数を音声周波数に変える。", "音声周波数を中間周波数に変える。", "受信周波数を音声周波数に変える。"], "a": 0, "e": "<b>スーパヘテロダイン受信機とは：<br>\n      受信した高周波信号（RF）を局部発振器と混合器によって中間周波数（IF）に変換し、その後に増幅・検波・復調する構成の受信機です。<br>\n      <br>\n      周波数変換部の役割：<br>\n      受信周波数（RF）と局部発振周波数（LO）の差（または和）をとることで、<br>\n      一定の中間周波数（IF）に変換しやすくするのが目的。<br>\n      これにより、高性能で選択度・感度に優れた受信が可能になります。</b>", "ee": "A superheterodyne receiver mixes the received RF signal with a local oscillator to convert it to an intermediate frequency (IF), then amplifies, detects and demodulates it.<br>The frequency conversion section takes the difference (or sum) of the received frequency (RF) and the local oscillator frequency (LO) to produce a fixed IF. This gives high performance with good selectivity and sensitivity.", "eg": false, "eq": "What is the function of the frequency conversion section of a superheterodyne receiver?", "eo": ["Converts the received frequency to the intermediate frequency.", "Converts the intermediate frequency to audio frequency.", "Converts audio frequency to the intermediate frequency.", "Converts the received frequency to audio frequency."], "v": [97, 98, 99, 100, 88, 345, 392, 304]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "過去問 令和3年10月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_musen_0310/", "k": "24", "al": [], "q": "FM（F3E）送受信機において、電波が発射されるのは、次のうちどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["電源スイッチを接(ON)にしたとき。", "プレストークボタンを押したとき。", "スケルチを動作させたとき。", "プレストークボタンを離したとき。"], "a": 1, "e": "<b>\n      FM（F3E）送受信機は、プレストーク（PTT：Push-To-Talk）方式を採用しており、次のような仕組みになっています：<br>\n      プレストークボタンを押す（PTT ON）<br>\n      　→ 送信モードになる<br>\n      　→ 電波が発射される<br>\n      <br>\n      プレストークボタンを離す<br>\n      　→ 受信モードになる<br></b>", "ee": "FM (F3E) transceivers use press-to-talk (PTT):<br>Press the PTT button → transmit mode → radio waves are emitted.<br>Release the PTT button → receive mode.", "eg": false, "eq": "In an FM (F3E) transceiver, when are radio waves emitted?", "eo": ["When the power switch is turned ON.", "When the press-to-talk button is pressed.", "When the squelch is activated.", "When the press-to-talk button is released."], "v": [90, 130, 131, 138, 393, 394, 420, 304, 418]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "過去問 令和4年2月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_musen_0402/", "k": "13", "al": [{"s": "例題集 No.1", "k": "13", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no1/"}], "q": "電気に関する単位で、誤っているのはどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["電流〔A〕", "インダクタンス〔Wb〕", "静電容量〔F〕", "抵抗〔Ω〕"], "a": 1, "e": "<b>\n      電流（アンペア）：𝐴 → 正しい<br>\n      インダクタンス（インダクタンスはヘンリー）：𝐻 → 誤り<br>\n      静電容量（ファラド）：𝐹 → 正しい<br>\n      抵抗（オーム）：Ω → 正しい<br></b>", "ee": "Current (ampere): A → correct<br>Inductance: the unit is the henry, H → INCORRECT (Wb, the weber, is the unit of magnetic flux)<br>Capacitance (farad): F → correct<br>Resistance (ohm): Ω → correct", "eg": false, "eq": "Which electrical unit is INCORRECT?", "eo": ["Current [A]", "Inductance [Wb]", "Capacitance [F]", "Resistance [Ω]"], "v": [10, 435, 2, 8, 14, 333, 383]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "過去問 令和4年2月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_musen_0402/", "k": "14", "al": [], "q": "電界効果トランジスタ（FET）の電極と一般の接合形トランジスタの電極の組合せで、その働きが対応しているのはどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["ドレイン　―　ベース", "ゲート　　―　ベース", "ドレイン　―　エミッタ", "ソース　　―　コレクタ"], "a": 1, "e": "<div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/ccdc41e4f0.png\" \n          alt=\"接合型トランジスタと接合型FET\"  >\n      </div>\n      <br>\n      <b>トランジスタとFETは、ベースに対応する端子が「ゲート」、コレクタに対応する端子が「ドレイン」、エミッタに対応する端子が「ソース」と呼ばれます。</b>", "ee": "<div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/ccdc41e4f0.png\" \n          alt=\"接合型トランジスタと接合型FET\"  >\n      </div> Between a transistor and an FET: the terminal corresponding to the base is the gate, the collector corresponds to the drain, and the emitter corresponds to the source.", "eg": false, "eq": "Which pairing of a field-effect transistor (FET) electrode with a regular junction transistor electrode has corresponding functions?", "eo": ["Drain – Base", "Gate – Base", "Drain – Emitter", "Source – Collector"], "v": [117, 118, 339, 119, 335, 392, 436]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "過去問 令和4年2月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_musen_0402/", "k": "15", "al": [], "q": "図に示すアンテナの名称と𝑙の長さの組合せで、正しいのはどれか。", "x": "<div>\n    <img loading=\"lazy\" \n      src=\"img/8674922680.png\" \n      alt=\"3陸特_無線工学No3_問題15\"  >\n  </div>", "o": ["ホイップアンテナ　1/4波長", "ホイップアンテナ　1/2波長", "スリーブアンテナ　1/4波長", "スリーブアンテナ　1/2波長"], "a": 2, "e": "<b>導体棒（上部）：主に放射素子として機能<br>\n      円筒状導体（下部）：給電点周囲を覆う構造で、反射素子やグランド面の代替として機能<br>\n      同軸ケーブル：円筒導体の中心を通っており、内側導体が導体棒に接続されている<br>\n      このような構造は、λ/4の円筒導体（スリーブ）が仮想的な接地面として働き、λ/2ダイポールアンテナの片側を模擬する形で、インピーダンス整合や放射効率を向上させる工夫がされています。", "ee": "Conductor rod (top): acts mainly as the radiating element.<br>Cylindrical conductor (bottom, the sleeve): covers the feed point and acts in place of a reflector/ground plane.<br>Coaxial cable: runs through the center of the sleeve, with the inner conductor connected to the rod.<br>The λ/4 sleeve works as a virtual ground plane, simulating one half of a λ/2 dipole, which improves impedance matching and radiation efficiency.", "eg": false, "eq": "Which combination of the antenna name and length l shown in the figure is correct?", "eo": ["Whip antenna, 1/4 wavelength", "Whip antenna, 1/2 wavelength", "Sleeve antenna, 1/4 wavelength", "Sleeve antenna, 1/2 wavelength"], "v": [322, 339, 22, 27, 330, 386, 329]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "過去問 令和4年2月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_musen_0402/", "k": "16", "al": [], "q": "電波の伝搬速度は、光の速さと同じで1秒間に3 × (𝐴) メートルである。また、同一波形が1秒間に繰り返される回数を (𝐵) という。", "x": "", "o": ["(A) 10<sup>8</sup>, (B) 周期", "(A) 10<sup>8</sup>, (B) 周波数", "(A) 10<sup>10</sup>, (B) 周波数", "(A) 10<sup>10</sup>, (B) 周期"], "a": 1, "e": "<b>\n      光速（電波の伝搬速度）＝ 約 3 × 10<sup>8</sup>m/s<br>\n      同一波形が1秒間に繰り返される回数 ＝ 周波数（frequency）</b>", "ee": "Speed of light (propagation speed of radio waves) ≈ 3 × 10<sup>8</sup> m/s.<br>The number of times the same waveform repeats in one second = frequency.", "eg": false, "eq": "Radio waves propagate at the speed of light: 3 × (A) meters per second. The number of times the same waveform repeats in one second is called (B).", "eo": ["(A) 10<sup>8</sup>, (B) period", "(A) 10<sup>8</sup>, (B) frequency", "(A) 10<sup>10</sup>, (B) frequency", "(A) 10<sup>10</sup>, (B) period"], "v": [39, 440, 42, 40, 41, 138, 374, 396, 438, 439, 441, 437]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "過去問 令和4年2月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_musen_0402/", "k": "17", "al": [], "q": "鉛蓄電池の取扱い上の注意として、誤っているのはどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["過放電させないこと。", "日光の当たる場所に置かないこと。", "電解液が少なくなったら蒸留水を補充すること。", "常に過充電すること。"], "a": 3, "e": "<b>鉛蓄電池は過放電・過充電ともに劣化の原因となるため避けるべきです。<br>\n      日光や高温は劣化を早めるため正しい。<br>\n      電解液が減ったら蒸留水を補充するのも、正しい対応。<br>\n      <br>\n      過充電はバッテリー寿命を縮め、ガス発生や膨張などの原因になります。</b>", "ee": "Both over-discharge and overcharge damage a lead-acid battery, so avoid them. Keeping it out of sunlight and heat is correct, since heat speeds up deterioration. Topping up with distilled water when the electrolyte is low is also correct. Overcharging shortens battery life and causes gassing and swelling.", "eg": false, "eq": "Which is INCORRECT as a precaution for handling lead-acid batteries?", "eo": ["Do not over-discharge it.", "Do not place it in direct sunlight.", "Top up with distilled water when the electrolyte gets low.", "Always overcharge it."], "v": [44, 543, 50, 51, 52, 53, 479, 54, 333, 350, 477, 478, 480, 481, 482]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "過去問 令和4年2月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_musen_0402/", "k": "18", "al": [], "q": "アナログ方式の回路計（テスタ）で直流抵抗を測定するときの準備の手順で正しいのはどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["測定レンジを選ぶ → 0[Ω]調整をする → テストリードを短絡する。", "0[Ω]調整をする → 測定レンジを選ぶ → テストリードを短絡する。", "測定レンジを選ぶ → テストリードを短絡する → 0[Ω]調整をする。", "テストリードを短絡する → 0[Ω]調整をする → 測定レンジを選ぶ。"], "a": 2, "e": "<b>アナログテスタで抵抗を測る前の基本手順は以下の通り：<br>\n      測定レンジを選ぶ（適切なΩレンジに切り替える）<br>\n      テストリード（テスト棒）を短絡（接触）する<br>\n      ゼロオーム調整（0Ω校正）をする<br>\n      <br>\n      最初にレンジを選ばないと、調整する基準が変わってしまう<br>\n      ゼロオーム調整は、テストリードを短絡して行う必要がある<br></b>", "ee": "Basic steps before measuring resistance with an analog tester:<br>1. Select the measurement range (switch to a suitable Ω range).<br>2. Short the test leads together.<br>3. Do the zero-ohm (0 Ω) adjustment.<br>If you don't select the range first, the reference you adjusted to changes. The zero-ohm adjustment must be done with the test leads shorted.", "eg": false, "eq": "What is the correct preparation procedure when measuring DC resistance with an analog circuit tester?", "eo": ["Select the range → zero-ohm adjust → short the test leads.", "Zero-ohm adjust → select the range → short the test leads.", "Select the range → short the test leads → zero-ohm adjust.", "Short the test leads → zero-ohm adjust → select the range."], "v": [59, 322, 2, 9, 61, 62, 63, 306, 331, 442, 443]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "過去問 令和4年2月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_musen_0402/", "k": "19", "al": [], "q": "AM（A3E）通信方式と比べたときのFM（F3E）通信方式の一般的な特徴で、正しいのはどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["占有周波数帯幅が広い。", "搬送波を抑圧している。", "雑音の影響を受けやすい。", "装置の回路構成が簡単である。"], "a": 0, "e": "<b>FMは高音質・ノイズ耐性に優れる一方、広い周波数帯域を必要とするのが特徴です。</b>", "ee": "FM offers high audio quality and good noise resistance, but it needs a wide frequency bandwidth.", "eg": false, "eq": "Which is a correct general characteristic of FM (F3E) communication compared with AM (A3E)?", "eo": ["The occupied bandwidth is wider.", "The carrier is suppressed.", "It is easily affected by noise.", "The circuit configuration of the equipment is simple."], "v": [72, 76, 73, 322, 334, 1, 21, 74, 75, 308, 328, 332, 340, 397, 413, 444]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "過去問 令和4年2月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_musen_0402/", "k": "20", "al": [{"s": "過去問 令和3年10月", "k": "20", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_musen_0310/"}], "q": "次の記述は、アナログ通信方式と比べたときのデジタル通信方式の一般的な特徴について述べたものである。誤っているものを下の番号から選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["雑音の影響を受けにくい。", "ネットワークやコンピュータとの親和性がよい。", "信号処理による遅延がない。", "受信側で誤り訂正を行うことができる。"], "a": 2, "e": "<b>デジタル通信は、以下のような特徴を持ちます：</b>\n      <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/6eacf77afa.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No2_解答20\"  >\n      </div>\n      <b>よって、「信号処理による遅延がない。」が誤りとなります。</b>", "ee": "Digital communication has these characteristics: <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/6eacf77afa.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No2_解答20\"  >\n      </div> Therefore \"there is no delay due to signal processing\" is the incorrect statement.", "eg": false, "eq": "The following describe general characteristics of digital communication compared with analog communication. Choose the INCORRECT one.", "eo": ["It is less affected by noise.", "It has good compatibility with networks and computers.", "There is no delay due to signal processing.", "Error correction can be performed on the receiving side."], "v": [76, 77, 79, 80, 334, 375, 75, 78, 305, 306, 307, 308, 319, 321, 328, 332, 333, 340, 304, 317]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "過去問 令和4年2月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_musen_0402/", "k": "21", "al": [], "q": "次の記述は、デジタル変調について述べたものである。(　　　)内に入れるべき字句は次のうちどれか。<br>\n    <br>\n    FSKは、ベースバンド信号に応じて搬送波の周波数を切り替える方式である。また、4値FSKは、1回の変調（シンボル）で(　　　)ビットの情報を伝送できる。", "x": "", "o": ["4", "3", "2", "1"], "a": 2, "e": "<b>4値（4段階）のFSKでは、1シンボルあたり2ビットの情報を伝送できます。</b>", "ee": "4-level FSK carries 2 bits of information per symbol (4 = 2²).", "eg": false, "eq": "The following describes digital modulation. Which word fills the blank? FSK switches the carrier frequency according to the baseband signal. 4-level FSK can transmit ( ) bits of information per modulation (symbol).", "eo": [null, null, null, null], "v": [433, 42, 73, 315, 65, 81, 82, 305, 316, 321, 331, 336, 415, 304, 314, 327, 416]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "過去問 令和4年2月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_musen_0402/", "k": "22", "al": [], "q": "図は、デジタル無線送信装置の概念図例を示したものである。 (　　　)内に入れるべき字句を下の番号から選べ。", "x": "<div>\n    <img loading=\"lazy\" \n      src=\"img/c8896f18f9.png\" \n      alt=\"3陸特_過去問-無線工学令和4年2月-問題22\"  >\n  </div>", "o": ["A/D変換器", "周波数変調器", "IDC回路", "AFC回路"], "a": 0, "e": "", "ee": "In a digital transmitter, the analog voice from the microphone must first be converted into a digital signal. The device that does this is an A/D converter (Analog-to-Digital Converter).", "eg": true, "eq": "The figure is an example conceptual diagram of a digital radio transmitter. Choose the item that fills the blank.", "eo": ["A/D converter", "Frequency modulator", "IDC circuit (instantaneous deviation control)", "AFC circuit (automatic frequency control)"], "v": [68, 93, 94, 95, 315, 1, 306, 316, 319, 330, 391, 314, 317, 329, 417]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "過去問 令和4年2月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_musen_0402/", "k": "23", "al": [], "q": "スーパヘテロダイン受信機において、近接周波数による混信を軽減するには、どのようにするのが最も効果的か。", "x": "", "o": ["AGC 回路を断（OFF）にする。", "中間周波増幅器に適切な特性の帯域フィルタ（BPF）を用いる。", "高周波増幅器の利得を下げる。", "局部発振器に水晶発振器を用いる。"], "a": 1, "e": "", "ee": "Selectivity against adjacent frequencies is set mainly in the IF amplifier stage. Putting a band-pass filter (BPF) with suitable characteristics in the IF amplifier removes signals just outside the wanted channel, which is the most effective way to cut adjacent-channel interference.", "eg": true, "eq": "In a superheterodyne receiver, what is the most effective way to reduce interference from adjacent frequencies?", "eo": ["Turn the AGC circuit OFF.", "Use a band-pass filter (BPF) with suitable characteristics in the IF amplifier.", "Lower the gain of the RF amplifier.", "Use a crystal oscillator as the local oscillator."], "v": [102, 103, 105, 106, 109, 88, 398, 483, 1, 104, 107, 108, 110, 376, 421, 445, 317, 419]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "過去問 令和4年2月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_musen_0402/", "k": "24", "al": [{"s": "例題集 No.1", "k": "24", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no1/"}], "q": "FM(F3E)送受信機において、電波が発射されるのはどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["電源スイッチを接(ON)にしたとき。", "スケルチを動作させたとき。", "プレストークボタンを離したとき。", "プレストークボタンを押したとき。"], "a": 3, "e": "<b>\n      FM（F3E）送受信機は、プレストーク（PTT：Push-To-Talk）方式を採用しており、次のような仕組みになっています：<br>\n      プレストークボタンを押す（PTT ON）<br>\n      　→ 送信モードになる<br>\n      　→ 電波が発射される<br>\n      <br>\n      プレストークボタンを離す<br>\n      　→ 受信モードになる<br></b>", "ee": "FM (F3E) transceivers use press-to-talk (PTT):<br>Press the PTT button → transmit mode → radio waves are emitted.<br>Release the PTT button → receive mode.", "eg": false, "eq": "In an FM (F3E) transceiver, when are radio waves emitted?", "eo": ["When the power switch is turned ON.", "When the squelch is activated.", "When the press-to-talk button is released.", "When the press-to-talk button is pressed."], "v": [90, 130, 131, 138, 393, 394, 420, 418]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和3年6月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0306/", "k": "1", "al": [], "q": "無線局の無線設備の変更の工事の許可を受けた免許人は、総務省令で定める場合を除き、どのような手続きをとった後でなければ、許可に係る無線設備を運用してはならないか。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["当該工事の結果が許可の内容に適合している旨を総務大臣に届け出た後", "総務大臣に運用開始の予定期日を届け出た後", "工事が完了した後、その運用について総務大臣の許可を受けた後", "総務大臣の検査を受け、当該工事の結果が許可の内容に適合していると認められた後"], "a": 3, "e": "", "ee": "After permitted modification work, the equipment may not be operated until the Minister's inspection confirms the results conform to the permission (except in cases set by MIC ordinance). (Radio Act, Art. 18)", "eg": true, "eq": "A licensee who has received permission to make changes (construction work) to a station's radio equipment may not operate that equipment until after which procedure, except in cases specified by MIC ordinance?", "eo": ["After notifying the Minister that the results of the work conform to the permitted content", "After notifying the Minister of the scheduled start date of operation", "After the work is completed and the Minister grants permission for its operation", "After undergoing the Minister's inspection and the results of the work are recognized as conforming to the permitted content"], "v": [140, 158, 159, 211, 212, 139, 146, 162, 323, 161, 172, 175, 176, 177, 178, 210, 302, 306, 308, 318, 337, 377, 378, 399, 422, 446, 304, 312, 324]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和3年6月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0306/", "k": "2", "al": [], "q": "固定局（免許の有効期間が1年以内であるものを除く。）の再免許の申請は、どの期間内に行わなければならないか。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["免許の有効期間満了前1箇月まで", "免許の有効期間満了前2箇月まで", "免許の有効期間満了前2箇月以上3箇月を超えない期間", "免許の有効期間満了前3箇月以上6箇月を超えない期間"], "a": 3, "e": "", "ee": "For stations such as fixed stations and land mobile stations, renewal applications must be filed between 6 months and 3 months before the license expires. (Radio Station License Procedure Regulations, Art. 18)", "eg": true, "eq": "Within what period must an application for license renewal of a fixed station be made (excluding licenses valid for 1 year or less)?", "eo": ["Up to 1 month before the license expires", "Up to 2 months before the license expires", "A period from 3 months to 2 months before the license expires", "A period from 6 months to 3 months before the license expires"], "v": [153, 149, 239, 145, 154, 156, 303, 306, 307, 337, 341, 343, 347, 400, 304, 314, 346, 535]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和3年6月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0306/", "k": "3", "al": [], "q": "次の記述は、電波の質について述べたものである。電波法の規定に照らし、［　　］内に入れるべき字句を下の番号から選べ。<br>\n送信設備に使用する電波の周波数の偏差及び幅、［　　］電波の質は、総務省令で定めるところに適合するものでなければならない。", "x": "", "o": ["高調波の強度等", "空中線電力の偏差等", "変調度等", "信号対雑音比等"], "a": 0, "e": "<b>電波の質とは、「周波数の偏差」、「周波数の幅」、「高調波の強度」と定義されています。(電波法 第28条)</b>", "ee": "The quality of radio waves is defined as the frequency deviation, the frequency bandwidth, and the harmonic intensity. (Radio Act, Art. 28)", "eg": false, "eq": "The following concerns the quality of radio waves. Under the Radio Act, choose what fills the blank. The quality of radio waves used by transmitting equipment, such as the frequency deviation and bandwidth, [ ], must conform to MIC ordinance.", "eo": ["harmonic intensity, etc.", "antenna power deviation, etc.", "modulation depth, etc.", "signal-to-noise ratio, etc."], "v": [184, 186, 159, 179, 401, 42, 137, 181, 183, 315, 323, 356, 138, 160, 178, 180, 182, 305, 306, 310, 316, 319, 320, 321, 304, 314, 317, 326, 357]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和3年6月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0306/", "k": "4", "al": [{"s": "過去問 令和4年2月", "k": "4", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0402/"}], "q": "無線従事者は、免許証を失ったためにその再交付を受けた後、失った免許証を発見したときは、発見した日から何日以内にその免許証を総務大臣に返納しなければならないか。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["10日", "7日", "30日", "14日"], "a": 0, "e": "<b>免許証の再交付を受けた後、失った免許証を発見したときは、発見した日から10日以内にその免許証を総務大臣又は総合通信局長に返納しなければならない。(無線従事者規則 第51条)</b><br>", "ee": "After a reissue, if the lost license card is found, it must be returned to the Minister (or the Regional Bureau Director) within 10 days of finding it. (Radio Operator Regulations, Art. 51)", "eg": false, "eq": "After a radio operator lost their license card and received a reissue, if they find the lost card, within how many days of finding it must they return that card to the Minister?", "eo": ["10 days", "7 days", "30 days", "14 days"], "v": [141, 158, 148, 151, 152, 277, 306, 308, 325, 343, 369, 304, 311, 324]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和3年6月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0306/", "k": "5", "al": [{"s": "過去問 令和3年10月", "k": "4", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0310/"}], "q": "総務大臣が無線従事者の免許を与えないことができる者はどれか。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["刑法に規定する罪を犯し罰金以上の刑に処せられ、その執行を終わり、又はその執行を受けることがなくなった日から2年を経過しない者", "無線従事者の免許を取り消され、取消しの日から2年を経過しない者", "無線従事者の免許を取り消され、取消しの日から5年を経過しない者", "日本の国籍を有しない者"], "a": 1, "e": "<b>電波法又は放送法に規定する罪を犯し罰金以上の刑に処せられ、その執行を終わり、又はその執行を受けることがなくなった日から2年を経過しない者には、無線局の免許を与えないことができます(電波法 第5条)</b>", "ee": "A station license may be refused to a person who committed a crime under the Radio Act or Broadcast Act, was sentenced to a fine or heavier, and 2 years have not passed since the sentence was completed or ceased to apply. (Radio Act, Art. 5)", "eg": false, "eq": "To whom may the Minister refuse to grant a radio operator license?", "eo": ["A person who committed a crime under the Penal Code, was sentenced to a fine or heavier, and for whom 2 years have not passed since the sentence was completed or ceased to apply", "A person whose radio operator license was revoked, and 2 years have not passed since the revocation", "A person whose radio operator license was revoked, and 5 years have not passed since the revocation", "A person who does not have Japanese nationality"], "v": [141, 158, 202, 220, 201, 308, 145, 160, 214, 216, 217, 221, 222, 223, 306, 313, 338, 341, 344, 358, 379, 215, 218, 304, 309, 311, 535]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和3年6月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0306/", "k": "6", "al": [{"s": "過去問 令和4年2月", "k": "5", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0402/"}], "q": "第三級陸上特殊無線技士の資格を有する者が、陸上の無線局の空中線電力50ワット以下の無線設備（レーダー及び人工衛星局の中継により無線通信を行う無線局の多重無線設備を除く。）の外部の転換装置で電波の質に影響を及ぼさないものの技術操作を行うことができる周波数の電波はどれか。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["1,606.5kHzから4,000kHzまで", "4,000kHzから25,010kHzまで", "25,010kHzから960MHzまで", "960MHzから1,215MHzまで"], "a": 2, "e": "<b>第三級陸上特殊無線技士の技術操作範囲は、下記の通りです。<br>\n      固定局、基地局等の陸上の無線局（注１）の無線設備（レーダー及び人工衛星局の中継により無線通信を行う無線局の多重無線設備を除く。）で次のもの<br>\n      － ５０Ｗ以下の無線設備で２５，０１０ｋＨｚ～９６０ＭＨｚまでの周波数の電波を使用するもの<br>\n      － １００Ｗ以下の無線設備で１，２１５ＭＨｚ以上の周波数の電波を使用するもの<br>\n      (注１)陸上の無線局とは、海岸局、海岸地球局、船舶局、船舶地球局、航空局、航空地球局、航空機局、航空機地球局、無線航行局及び基幹放送局<span>以外</span>の無線局をいう。</b><br>\n      <br>\n      <br><b>技術操作の操作範囲は下記の通りになります。(日本無線協会の資料引用)</b>\n      <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/8230859a63.png\" \n          alt=\"技術操作の操作範囲\"  >\n      </div>", "ee": "The technical operation scope of a 3rd Class Land Special Radio Operator covers equipment of land stations (note 1) such as fixed and base stations (excluding radar and multiplex equipment of stations relaying via satellite):<br>– Equipment of 50 W or less using 25,010 kHz to 960 MHz<br>– Equipment of 100 W or less using 1,215 MHz or higher<br>(Note 1) \"Land stations\" means stations other than coast, coast earth, ship, ship earth, aeronautical, aeronautical earth, aircraft, aircraft earth, radionavigation and core broadcasting stations.<br>Operation scope chart (from the Japan Radio Association): <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/8230859a63.png\" \n          alt=\"技術操作の操作範囲\"  >\n      </div>", "eg": false, "eq": "For a person holding the 3rd Class Land Special Radio Operator qualification, on which frequency range may they perform technical operation of external switching devices that do not affect radio wave quality, on land-station equipment with antenna power of 50 W or less (excluding radar and multiplex equipment of stations relaying via satellite)?", "eo": ["1,606.5 kHz to 4,000 kHz", "4,000 kHz to 25,010 kHz", "25,010 kHz to 960 MHz", "960 MHz to 1,215 MHz"], "v": [144, 247, 186, 244, 140, 143, 179, 248, 249, 42, 139, 338, 536, 138, 227, 236, 246, 306, 307, 310, 328, 337, 342, 402, 304, 309]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和3年6月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0306/", "k": "7", "al": [], "q": "無線局を運用する場合においては、遭難通信を行う場合を除き、電波の型式及び周波数は、どの書類に記載されたところによらなければならないか。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["免許状", "無線局事項書の写し", "免許証", "無線局の免許の申請書の写し"], "a": 0, "e": "<b>電波の型式及び周波数は免許状に記載があり、記載されている内容で運用する必要があります。</b>\n      <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/d7aa226ab0.png\" \n          alt=\"法規(令和3年6月_解答7\"  >\n      </div>", "ee": "The emission type and frequency are written on the station license (免許状), and the station must be operated as written there. <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/d7aa226ab0.png\" \n          alt=\"法規(令和3年6月_解答7\"  >\n      </div>", "eg": false, "eq": "When operating a radio station (except for distress communication), the emission type and frequency must follow what is stated in which document?", "eo": ["Station license (免許状)", "Copy of the station particulars form", "Operator license card (免許証)", "Copy of the station license application"], "v": [262, 258, 42, 139, 147, 148, 157, 138, 145, 188, 210, 265, 266, 306, 307, 310, 318, 337, 348, 304]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和3年6月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0306/", "k": "8", "al": [], "q": "総務大臣は、無線局の発射する電波の質が総務省令で定めるものに適合していないと認めるときは、その無線局に対してどのような処分を行うことができるか。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["無線局の免許を取り消す。", "空中線の撤去を命ずる。", "臨時に電波の発射の停止を命ずる。", "周波数又は空中線電力の指定を変更する。"], "a": 2, "e": "<b>「総務大臣は、無線局の発射する電波の質が総務省令で定める技術基準に適合していないと認めるときは、その無線局に対し、臨時に電波の発射の停止を命ずることができる。」(電波法 第72条)</b>", "ee": "\"When the Minister finds that the quality of radio waves emitted by a station does not meet the technical standards set by MIC ordinance, the Minister may order that station to temporarily stop emitting radio waves.\" (Radio Act, Art. 72)", "eg": false, "eq": "When the Minister finds that the quality of radio waves emitted by a station does not conform to MIC ordinance, what action can the Minister take against that station?", "eo": ["Revoke the station license.", "Order removal of the antenna.", "Temporarily order the station to stop emitting radio waves.", "Change the designated frequency or antenna power."], "v": [186, 158, 159, 179, 202, 42, 139, 185, 323, 353, 378, 380, 131, 138, 145, 174, 175, 178, 197, 198, 203, 206, 306, 307, 313, 304]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和3年6月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0306/", "k": "9", "al": [{"s": "過去問 令和4年2月", "k": "9", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0402/"}], "q": "無線局の免許人が電波法又は電波法に基づく命令に違反したときに総務大臣が行うことができる処分はどれか。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["無線局の運用の停止", "通信の相手方又は通信事項の制限", "電波の型式の制限", "再免許の拒否"], "a": 0, "e": "<b>「総務大臣は、無線局がこの法律又はこれに基づく命令の規定に違反して運用されているとき、又はそのおそれがあるときは、その無線局の運用の停止を命ずることができる。」(電波法 第76条)</b>", "ee": "\"When a station is operated in violation of this Act or orders based on it, or there is a risk of this, the Minister may order suspension of the station's operation.\" (Radio Act, Art. 76)", "eg": false, "eq": "What action can the Minister take when a station licensee violates the Radio Act or orders based on it?", "eo": ["Suspension of station operation", "Restriction of communication counterparts or communication matters", "Restriction of emission type", "Refusal of license renewal"], "v": [158, 260, 137, 139, 146, 149, 261, 359, 138, 188, 198, 199, 200, 203, 204, 205, 210, 306, 307, 313, 349, 304]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和3年6月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0306/", "k": "10", "al": [], "q": "無線従事者が総務大臣から3箇月以内の期間を定めてその業務に従事することを停止されることがあるのはどの場合か。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["免許証を失ったとき。", "無線通信の業務に従事することがなくなったとき。", "電波法に違反したとき。", "無線局の運用を休止したとき。"], "a": 2, "e": "", "ee": "The Minister can suspend a radio operator from their duties for up to 3 months when they violate the Radio Act or orders/dispositions based on it. (Radio Act, Art. 79)", "eg": true, "eq": "In which case may the Minister suspend a radio operator from their duties for a set period of up to 3 months?", "eo": ["When they lose their license card.", "When they no longer engage in radio communication duties.", "When they violate the Radio Act.", "When station operation is suspended."], "v": [141, 143, 158, 137, 139, 148, 199, 203, 207, 210, 233, 234, 303, 306, 318, 323, 325, 343, 347, 304]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和3年6月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0306/", "k": "11", "al": [], "q": "無線局の免許状を1箇月以内に総務大臣に返納しなければならないのはどの場合か。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["無線局の運用の停止を命じられたとき。", "免許状を破損し、又は汚したとき。", "無線局の運用を休止したとき。", "無線局の免許がその効力を失ったとき。"], "a": 3, "e": "", "ee": "When a station license loses its validity (e.g. the station is closed or the license expires), the former licensee must return the station license within 1 month. (Radio Act, Art. 24)", "eg": true, "eq": "In which case must a station license be returned to the Minister within 1 month?", "eo": ["When ordered to suspend station operation.", "When the license is damaged or soiled.", "When station operation is suspended.", "When the station license loses its validity."], "v": [158, 139, 147, 145, 152, 155, 203, 207, 210, 275, 303, 306, 313, 318, 325, 343, 353, 423, 304]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和3年6月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0306/", "k": "12", "al": [], "q": "無線局の免許人は、主任無線従事者を選任し、又は解任したときは、どうしなければならないか。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["速やかに総務大臣の承認を受ける。", "遅滞なく、その旨を総務大臣に届け出る。", "2週間以内にその旨を総務大臣に届け出る。", "1箇月以内にその旨を総務大臣に報告する。"], "a": 1, "e": "", "ee": "When a chief radio operator is appointed or dismissed, the licensee must notify the Minister without delay. No approval is needed. (Radio Act, Art. 39)", "eg": true, "eq": "When a licensee appoints or dismisses a chief radio operator, what must they do?", "eo": ["Promptly obtain the Minister's approval.", "Notify the Minister without delay.", "Notify the Minister within 2 weeks.", "Report to the Minister within 1 month."], "v": [142, 158, 162, 166, 167, 139, 146, 308, 163, 164, 169, 170, 303, 306, 313, 343, 403, 304, 312]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和3年10月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0310/", "k": "1", "al": [], "q": "次の記述は、電波法の目的である。〔　　〕内に入れるべき字句を下の番号から選べ。<br>\n    この法律は、電波の公平かつ〔　　〕な利用を確保することによって、公共の福祉を増進することを目的とする。", "x": "", "o": ["能率的", "能動的", "積極的", "経済的"], "a": 0, "e": "", "ee": "Article 1 of the Radio Act: \"This law aims to promote public welfare by ensuring fair and efficient (能率的) use of radio waves.\"", "eg": true, "eq": "The following is the purpose of the Radio Act. Choose what fills the blank. \"This law aims to promote public welfare by ensuring fair and [ ] use of radio waves.\"", "eo": ["efficient", "active", "proactive", "economical"], "v": [283, 137, 282, 315, 485, 486, 487, 138, 280, 281, 284, 285, 305, 306, 316, 319, 447, 448, 304, 314, 317]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和3年10月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0310/", "k": "2", "al": [], "q": "再免許を受けた陸上移動局の免許の有効期間は何年か。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["10年", "5年", "4年", "3年"], "a": 1, "e": "", "ee": "The license validity period of a land mobile station is 5 years, including after renewal. (Radio Act, Art. 13 and its Enforcement Regulations)", "eg": true, "eq": "How many years is the license validity period of a land mobile station that has received a renewed license?", "eo": ["10 years", "5 years", "4 years", "3 years"], "v": [237, 153, 149, 145, 306, 308, 370, 304, 535]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和3年10月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0310/", "k": "5", "al": [], "q": "無線従事者は、免許証を失ったためにその再交付を受けた後、失った免許証を発見したときはどうしなければならないか。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["速やかに発見した免許証を廃棄する。", "発見した日から10日以内にその旨を総務大臣に届け出る。", "発見した日から10日以内に再交付を受けた免許証を総務大臣に返納する。", "発見した日から10日以内に発見した免許証を総務大臣に返納する。"], "a": 3, "e": "", "ee": "If the lost card turns up after a reissue, the found (old) card must be returned to the Minister within 10 days of finding it. (Radio Operator Regulations, Art. 51)", "eg": true, "eq": "After a radio operator lost their license card and received a reissue, what must they do if they find the lost card?", "eo": ["Promptly destroy the found card.", "Notify the Minister of the fact within 10 days of finding it.", "Return the reissued card to the Minister within 10 days of finding the old one.", "Return the found card to the Minister within 10 days of finding it."], "v": [141, 158, 162, 167, 148, 151, 152, 276, 277, 306, 308, 325, 343, 304, 311, 312, 324]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和3年10月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0310/", "k": "6", "al": [], "q": "「無線従事者」の定義として、正しいものはどれか。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["無線設備の操作又はその監督を行う者であって、総務大臣の免許を受けたものをいう。", "無線設備の操作を行う者であって、無線局に配置されたものをいう。", "無線従事者国家試験に合格した者をいう。", "無線設備の操作を行う者をいう。"], "a": 0, "e": "", "ee": "Radio Act Art. 2: a radio operator is \"a person who operates radio equipment or supervises its operation, and who has received a license from the Minister.\"", "eg": true, "eq": "Which is the correct definition of \"radio operator\" (無線従事者)?", "eo": ["A person who operates radio equipment or supervises its operation, and who has received a license from the Minister.", "A person who operates radio equipment and is assigned to a radio station.", "A person who has passed the national radio operator exam.", "A person who operates radio equipment."], "v": [141, 140, 158, 235, 139, 322, 145, 250, 252, 254, 306, 307, 308, 313, 449, 488, 304, 309]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和3年10月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0310/", "k": "7", "al": [], "q": "無線局がなるべく擬似空中線回路を使用しなければならないのはどの場合か。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["他の無線局の通信に混信を与えるおそれがあるとき。", "工事設計書に記載した空中線を使用できないとき。", "無線設備の機器の試験又は調整を行うために運用するとき。", "総務大臣の行う無線局の検査のために運用するとき。"], "a": 2, "e": "", "ee": "Radio Act Art. 57: when operating a station to test or adjust radio equipment, a dummy antenna circuit should be used as much as possible, so the tests don't radiate radio waves and cause interference.", "eg": true, "eq": "In which case should a station use a dummy antenna circuit as much as possible?", "eo": ["When there is a risk of causing interference to other stations' communications.", "When the antenna listed in the construction design document cannot be used.", "When operating to test or adjust radio equipment.", "When operating for a station inspection conducted by the Minister."], "v": [187, 263, 140, 158, 139, 185, 344, 63, 108, 172, 210, 306, 307, 313, 318, 320, 348, 349, 404, 451, 304, 450]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和3年10月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0310/", "k": "8", "al": [], "q": "総務大臣から無線従事者がその免許を取り消されることがあるのはどの場合か。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["不正な手段により無線従事者の免許を受けたとき。", "日本の国籍を有しない者となったとき。", "刑法に規定する罪を犯し、罰金以上の刑に処せられたとき。", "引き続き5年以上無線設備の操作を行わなかったとき。"], "a": 0, "e": "", "ee": "A radio operator license can be revoked if it was obtained by fraudulent means (also for Radio Act violations, or a serious mental/physical impairment). Losing nationality or 5 years without operating are not grounds. (Radio Act, Art. 79)", "eg": true, "eq": "In which case may the Minister revoke a radio operator's license?", "eo": ["When they obtained the radio operator license by fraudulent means.", "When they no longer hold Japanese nationality.", "When they commit a crime under the Penal Code and are sentenced to a fine or heavier.", "When they have not operated radio equipment for 5 consecutive years or more."], "v": [141, 224, 140, 158, 202, 220, 405, 145, 160, 214, 216, 217, 223, 250, 306, 307, 308, 318, 338, 341, 358, 215, 218, 304, 309, 535]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和3年10月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0310/", "k": "10", "al": [], "q": "無線局の免許人は、非常通信を行ったときは、どうしなければならないか。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["総務省令で定める手続により、総務大臣に報告する。", "直ちに総務大臣に電話連絡する。", "その通信の記録を作成し、1年間これを保存する。", "地方防災会議会長にその旨を通知する。"], "a": 0, "e": "", "ee": "After conducting emergency communication, the licensee must report it to the Minister following the procedure set by MIC ordinance. (Radio Act, Art. 80)", "eg": true, "eq": "What must a station licensee do after conducting emergency communication?", "eo": ["Report to the Minister following the procedure set by MIC ordinance.", "Immediately contact the Minister by telephone.", "Make a record of the communication and keep it for 1 year.", "Notify the chair of the local disaster prevention council."], "v": [301, 158, 159, 259, 455, 139, 146, 168, 323, 163, 274, 300, 302, 306, 307, 349, 452, 489, 490, 491, 304, 312]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和3年10月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0310/", "k": "11", "al": [], "q": "無線局の免許人は、免許状に記載した住所に変更を生じたときは、どうしなければならないか。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["総務大臣に無線設備の設置場所の変更の申請をする。", "遅滞なく、その旨を総務大臣に届け出る。", "免許状を訂正し、その旨を総務大臣に報告する。", "免許状を総務大臣に提出し、訂正を受ける。"], "a": 3, "e": "", "ee": "The licensee's address is one of the items written on the station license. When a stated item changes, the licensee must submit the license to the Minister and have it corrected. (Radio Act, Art. 21)", "eg": true, "eq": "What must a station licensee do when the address stated on the station license changes?", "eo": ["Apply to the Minister for a change of equipment installation location.", "Notify the Minister without delay.", "Correct the license and report it to the Minister.", "Submit the license to the Minister and have it corrected."], "v": [140, 158, 162, 166, 269, 139, 146, 147, 308, 156, 163, 175, 278, 296, 306, 348, 360, 409, 304, 312]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和3年10月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0310/", "k": "12", "al": [], "q": "無線局の免許人は、主任無線従事者を選任し、又は解任したときは、どうしなければならないか。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["遅滞なく、その旨を総務大臣に届け出る。", "1箇月以内にその旨を総務大臣に届け出る。", "2週間以内にその旨を総務大臣に報告する。", "速やかに総務大臣の承認を受ける。"], "a": 0, "e": "", "ee": "When a chief radio operator is appointed or dismissed, the licensee must notify the Minister without delay. No approval is needed. (Radio Act, Art. 39)", "eg": true, "eq": "When a licensee appoints or dismisses a chief radio operator, what must they do?", "eo": ["Notify the Minister without delay.", "Notify the Minister within 1 month.", "Report to the Minister within 2 weeks.", "Promptly obtain the Minister's approval."], "v": [142, 158, 162, 166, 167, 139, 146, 308, 163, 164, 169, 170, 303, 306, 313, 343, 403, 304, 312]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和4年2月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0402/", "k": "1", "al": [], "q": "無線局の免許状に記載される事項に該当しないものはどれか。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["通信の相手方及び通信事項", "空中線の型式及び構成", "無線設備の設置場所", "無線局の目的"], "a": 1, "e": "<b>無線局免許状には、空中線の型式及び構成が記載される欄がありません。</b>\n      <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/d7aa226ab0.png\" \n          alt=\"法規(令和4年2月_解答1\"  >\n      </div>", "ee": "The station license has no field for the antenna type and configuration. <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/d7aa226ab0.png\" \n          alt=\"法規(令和4年2月_解答1\"  >\n      </div>", "eg": false, "eq": "Which is NOT an item stated on a station license?", "eo": ["Communication counterparts and communication matters", "Antenna type and configuration", "Installation location of the radio equipment", "Purpose of the station"], "v": [140, 260, 269, 139, 147, 185, 261, 21, 188, 280, 306, 310, 348, 349, 354, 381, 304]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和4年2月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0402/", "k": "2", "al": [], "q": "陸上移動業務の無線局（免許の有効期間が1年以内であるものを除く。）の再免許の申請は、どの期間内に行わなければならないか。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["免許の有効期間満了前3箇月以上6箇月を超えない期間", "免許の有効期間満了前2箇月以上3箇月を超えない期間", "免許の有効期間満了前2箇月まで", "免許の有効期間満了前1箇月まで"], "a": 0, "e": "", "ee": "For stations such as land mobile stations, renewal applications must be filed between 6 months and 3 months before the license expires. (Radio Station License Procedure Regulations, Art. 18)", "eg": true, "eq": "Within what period must an application for license renewal of a land mobile service station be made (excluding licenses valid for 1 year or less)?", "eo": ["A period from 6 months to 3 months before the license expires", "A period from 3 months to 2 months before the license expires", "Up to 2 months before the license expires", "Up to 1 month before the license expires"], "v": [238, 153, 139, 149, 145, 154, 156, 303, 306, 307, 337, 341, 343, 347, 400, 304, 314, 346, 535]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和4年2月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0402/", "k": "3", "al": [], "q": "電波の主搬送波の変調の型式が角度変調で周波数変調のもの、主搬送波を変調する信号の性質がアナログ信号である単一チャネルのものであって、伝送情報の型式が電話（音響の放送を含む。）の電波の型式を表示する記号はどれか。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["F3E", "F7E", "F8E", "A3E"], "a": 0, "e": "<div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/87bb210ce6.png\" \n          alt=\"技術操作の操作範囲\"  >\n      </div>", "ee": "Emission designation: F = frequency modulation (angle modulation); 3 = a single channel carrying an analog signal; E = telephony (including sound broadcasting). So the symbol is F3E. (A3E would be amplitude modulation.)<div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/87bb210ce6.png\" \n          alt=\"技術操作の操作範囲\"  >\n      </div>", "eg": true, "eq": "Which symbol designates the emission type where the main carrier is angle-modulated by frequency modulation, the modulating signal is a single analog channel, and the information transmitted is telephony (including sound broadcasting)?", "eo": [null, null, null, null], "v": [67, 189, 190, 192, 65, 138, 188, 191, 193, 194, 195, 196, 306, 336, 410, 453, 454, 304]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和4年2月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0402/", "k": "6", "al": [], "q": "総務大臣が無線従事者の免許を与えないことができる者は、無線従事者の免許を取り消され、取消しの日からどれほどの期間を経過しないものか。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["6箇月", "1年", "1年6箇月", "2年"], "a": 3, "e": "", "ee": "The Minister may refuse a radio operator license to a person whose license was revoked, until 2 years have passed since the revocation. (Radio Act, Art. 42)", "eg": true, "eq": "The Minister may refuse to grant a radio operator license to a person whose license was revoked, if how long has not yet passed since the revocation?", "eo": ["6 months", "1 year", "1 year 6 months", "2 years"], "v": [141, 158, 202, 201, 145, 222, 303, 306, 344, 347, 304, 309, 311, 535]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和4年2月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0402/", "k": "7", "al": [], "q": "一般通信方法における無線通信の原則として無線局運用規則に定める事項に該当するものはどれか。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["無線通信は、長時間継続して行ってはならない。", "無線通信を行う場合においては、暗語を使用してはならない。", "無線通信に使用する用語は、できる限り簡潔でなければならない。", "無線通信は、正確に行うものとし、通信上の誤りを知ったときは、通報の送信終了後一括して訂正しなければならない。"], "a": 2, "e": "", "ee": "Radio Station Operation Regulations, Art. 10: terms used in radio communication must be as concise as possible. The other choices are distortions: long transmissions are not banned outright, and errors must be corrected immediately, not all at once at the end.", "eg": true, "eq": "Which is a principle of radio communication in general communication methods specified in the Radio Station Operation Regulations?", "eo": ["Radio communication must not be carried on continuously for long periods.", "Code words must not be used in radio communication.", "Terms used in radio communication must be as concise as possible.", "Radio communication must be accurate; when an error is noticed, it must be corrected all at once after the message transmission ends."], "v": [293, 456, 143, 323, 457, 462, 290, 294, 295, 296, 297, 298, 306, 307, 318, 320, 333, 354, 381, 424, 458, 459, 460, 461, 463, 464, 304, 324]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和4年2月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0402/", "k": "8", "al": [{"s": "過去問 令和3年10月", "k": "9", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0310/"}], "q": "無線局の臨時検査（電波法第73条第5項の検査）において検査されることがあるものはどれか。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["無線従事者の知識及び技能", "無線従事者の資格及び員数", "無線従事者の勤務状況", "無線従事者の業務経歴"], "a": 1, "e": "<b>「総務大臣は、...必要があると認めるときは、その職員を無線局に派遣し、その無線設備等を検査させることができる。」<br>\n      ここで言う「無線設備等」には、無線設備、無線従事者の資格および員数、時計、書類が含まれます。</b>", "ee": "\"When the Minister finds it necessary, the Minister may send officials to a station to inspect its radio equipment, etc.\" Here \"radio equipment, etc.\" includes the radio equipment, the radio operators' qualifications and number, clocks, and documents.", "eg": false, "eq": "What may be inspected in an extraordinary inspection of a station (Radio Act Art. 73, Para. 5)?", "eo": ["The radio operators' knowledge and skills", "The radio operators' qualifications and number", "The radio operators' work status", "The radio operators' work history"], "v": [141, 173, 231, 232, 137, 139, 172, 227, 228, 229, 230, 306, 310, 304, 406, 407, 408]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和4年2月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0402/", "k": "10", "al": [], "q": "総務大臣から無線従事者がその免許を取り消されることがあるのはどの場合か。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["日本の国籍を有しない者となったとき。", "免許証を失ったとき。", "引き続き5年以上無線設備の操作を行わなかったとき。", "電波法に違反したとき。"], "a": 3, "e": "", "ee": "A radio operator license can be revoked when the operator violates the Radio Act. Losing the card, losing nationality, or not operating for 5 years are not grounds. (Radio Act, Art. 79)", "eg": true, "eq": "In which case may the Minister revoke a radio operator's license?", "eo": ["When they no longer hold Japanese nationality.", "When they lose their license card.", "When they have not operated radio equipment for 5 consecutive years or more.", "When they violate the Radio Act."], "v": [141, 140, 158, 202, 405, 137, 148, 145, 199, 223, 250, 306, 307, 318, 325, 338, 341, 358, 304, 309, 535]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和4年2月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0402/", "k": "11", "al": [], "q": "無線局の免許人は、無線従事者を選任し、又は解任したときは、どうしなければならないか。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["遅滞なく、その旨を総務大臣に届け出る。", "1箇月以内にその旨を総務大臣に報告する。", "2週間以内にその旨を総務大臣に届け出る。", "速やかに総務大臣の承認を受ける。"], "a": 0, "e": "", "ee": "When a radio operator is appointed or dismissed, the licensee must notify the Minister without delay. (Radio Act, Art. 51 applying Art. 39)", "eg": true, "eq": "When a licensee appoints or dismisses a radio operator, what must they do?", "eo": ["Notify the Minister without delay.", "Report to the Minister within 1 month.", "Notify the Minister within 2 weeks.", "Promptly obtain the Minister's approval."], "v": [141, 158, 162, 166, 167, 139, 146, 308, 163, 164, 169, 170, 303, 306, 313, 343, 403, 304, 312]}, {"c": "law", "s": "過去問 令和4年2月", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0402/", "k": "12", "al": [], "q": "無線局の免許人は、免許状に記載した事項に変更を生じたときは、どうしなければならないか。次のうちから選べ。", "x": "", "o": ["直ちに、その旨を総務大臣に届け出る。", "遅滞なく、その旨を総務大臣に報告する。", "総務大臣に免許状の再交付を申請する。", "免許状を総務大臣に提出し、訂正を受ける。"], "a": 3, "e": "", "ee": "When a matter stated on the station license changes, the licensee must submit the license to the Minister and have it corrected. (Radio Act, Art. 21)", "eg": true, "eq": "What must a station licensee do when a matter stated on the station license changes?", "eo": ["Notify the Minister immediately.", "Report to the Minister without delay.", "Apply to the Minister for reissue of the license.", "Submit the license to the Minister and have it corrected."], "v": [158, 162, 166, 139, 146, 147, 151, 168, 308, 156, 163, 175, 296, 306, 348, 360, 381, 409, 304, 312]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.3", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no3/", "k": "13", "al": [], "q": "図に示す回路の端子 ab 間の合成静電容量の値として正しいのはどれか。", "x": "<div>\n      <img loading=\"lazy\" \n        src=\"img/0b8d998644.png\" \n        alt=\"3陸特_無線工学No3_問題13\"  >\n    </div>", "o": ["11〔μF〕", "22〔μF〕", "33〔μF〕", "44〔μF〕"], "a": 0, "e": "<p><b>\n      抵抗C1とC2を直列に接続したときの合成容量C合成は以下の式で求めます：\n      </b></p>\n\n      <p>\\( \\frac{1}{C_{\\text{合成}}} = \\frac{1}{C_1} + \\frac{1}{C_2} \\)</p>\n      <p><b>\n      今回の回路では：<br></b></p>\n      <p>\\( C_1 = C_2 = 22\\mathrm{μF} \\)</p>\n      したがって、<br>\n      <p><b>\n      今回の回路では：<br></b></p>\n      <p>\\(\\frac{1}{C_{\\text{合成}}} = \\frac{1}{22} + \\frac{1}{22} = \\frac{2}{22} = \\frac{1}{11}\\)</p>\n      \n      <p>\\(C_{\\text{合成}} = 11\\,\\mathrm{μF}\\)</p>", "ee": "For capacitors C1 and C2 in series, the combined capacitance is: \\( \\frac{1}{C_{\\text{total}}} = \\frac{1}{C_1} + \\frac{1}{C_2} \\)<br>In this circuit \\( C_1 = C_2 = 22\\,\\mathrm{μF} \\), so: \\(\\frac{1}{C_{\\text{total}}} = \\frac{1}{22} + \\frac{1}{22} = \\frac{2}{22} = \\frac{1}{11}\\), giving \\(C_{\\text{total}} = 11\\,\\mathrm{μF}\\)", "eg": false, "eq": "What is the combined capacitance between terminals a and b in the circuit shown?", "eo": [null, null, null, null], "v": [11, 322, 1, 12, 330, 327, 329, 382]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.3", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no3/", "k": "14", "al": [], "q": "次の記述において（　　　）内に入れるべき字句の正しい組合せを下の番号から選べ。<br>\n  半導体は、周囲の温度が上昇すると、一般的にその電気抵抗が（A）し、内部を流れる電流は（B）する。", "x": "", "o": ["(A) 増加, (B) 減少", "(A) 増加, (B) 増加", "(A) 減少, (B) 増加", "(A) 減少, (B) 減少"], "a": 2, "e": "<b>半導体の温度特性について：<br>\n      半導体（例：シリコンやゲルマニウム）は、温度が上がるとキャリア（電子や正孔）の数が増加します。<br>\n      その結果、電気を流しやすくなり、抵抗値は下がります（＝A：減少）<br>\n      抵抗が小さくなると、同じ電圧でも、より多くの電流が流れる（＝B：増加）ことになります。<br>\n      <br>\n      純粋な抵抗の場合は、温度上昇により、金属中の自由電子が振動し抵抗値が上がり、電流値が下がります。<br>\n      特性が反対になりますので注意が必要です。<br>\n      </b>\n\n      <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/9ab211b6b1.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No3_解答14\"  >\n      </div>", "ee": "Temperature behavior of semiconductors: when the temperature of a semiconductor (e.g. silicon or germanium) rises, the number of carriers (electrons and holes) increases. It conducts more easily, so its resistance goes down (A: decreases). With lower resistance, more current flows at the same voltage (B: increases).<br>For an ordinary metal resistor it is the opposite: heat makes the free electrons vibrate more, so resistance rises and current falls. Don't mix the two up. <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/9ab211b6b1.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No3_解答14\"  >\n      </div>", "eg": false, "eq": "Choose the correct combination for the blanks. When the surrounding temperature of a semiconductor rises, its electrical resistance generally (A), and the current flowing through it (B).", "eo": ["(A) increases (B) decreases", "(A) increases (B) increases", "(A) decreases (B) increases", "(A) decreases (B) decreases"], "v": [15, 315, 322, 334, 339, 411, 2, 8, 16, 17, 18, 19, 305, 306, 316, 319, 383, 426, 427, 304, 314, 317]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.3", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no3/", "k": "15", "al": [], "q": "次の記述において（　　　）内に入れるべき字句の正しい組合せを下の番号から選べ。図のアンテナは、（A）アンテナと呼ばれる。電波の波長を λ で表したとき、導体棒の長さは（B）である。", "x": "<div>\n      <img loading=\"lazy\" \n        src=\"img/8674922680.png\" \n        alt=\"3陸特_無線工学No3_問題15\"  >\n    </div>", "o": ["(A) スリーブ, (B) λ / 4", "(A) スリーブ, (B) λ / 2", "(A) ホイップ, (B) λ / 4", "(A) ホイップ, (B) λ / 2"], "a": 0, "e": "<b>導体棒（上部）：主に放射素子として機能<br>\n      円筒状導体（下部）：給電点周囲を覆う構造で、反射素子やグランド面の代替として機能<br>\n      同軸ケーブル：円筒導体の中心を通っており、内側導体が導体棒に接続されている<br>\n      このような構造は、λ/4の円筒導体（スリーブ）が仮想的な接地面として働き、λ/2ダイポールアンテナの片側を模擬する形で、インピーダンス整合や放射効率を向上させる工夫がされています。", "ee": "Conductor rod (top): acts mainly as the radiating element.<br>Cylindrical conductor (bottom, the sleeve): covers the feed point and acts in place of a reflector/ground plane.<br>Coaxial cable: runs through the center of the sleeve, with the inner conductor connected to the rod.<br>The λ/4 sleeve works as a virtual ground plane, simulating one half of a λ/2 dipole, which improves impedance matching and radiation efficiency.", "eg": false, "eq": "Choose the correct combination for the blanks. The antenna in the figure is called a (A) antenna. When the wavelength is λ, the length of the conductor rod is (B).", "eo": ["(A) sleeve, (B) λ/4", "(A) sleeve, (B) λ/2", "(A) whip, (B) λ/4", "(A) whip, (B) λ/2"], "v": [26, 315, 322, 339, 27, 138, 305, 306, 316, 319, 386, 389, 492, 304, 314, 317, 329]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.3", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no3/", "k": "17", "al": [], "q": "次の記述は、ニッケルカドミウム蓄電池と比べたときの、リチウムイオン蓄電池の一般的な特徴について述べたものである。誤っているのはどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["同じ大きさであれば、高容量が得られる。", "電池 1 個の端子電圧は 1.2〔V〕より低い。", "自然に少しずつ放電する自己放電量が少ない。", "メモリー効果がないので、継ぎ足し充電ができる。"], "a": 1, "e": "<div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/bd0b9fa286.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No3_解答17\"  >\n      </div>", "ee": "A lithium-ion cell has a terminal voltage of about 3.6–3.7 V, much higher than the 1.2 V of a nickel-cadmium cell. \"Lower than 1.2 V\" is therefore incorrect. The other statements (high capacity, low self-discharge, no memory effect) are true.<div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/bd0b9fa286.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No3_解答17\"  >\n      </div>", "eg": true, "eq": "The following describe general characteristics of lithium-ion batteries compared with nickel-cadmium batteries. Which is INCORRECT?", "eo": ["For the same size, higher capacity is obtained.", "The terminal voltage of one cell is lower than 1.2 V.", "Self-discharge (gradual natural discharge) is small.", "There is no memory effect, so top-up charging is possible."], "v": [13, 55, 499, 43, 334, 350, 362, 493, 537, 56, 57, 305, 321, 332, 333, 340, 351, 374, 484, 494, 496, 497, 304, 495, 498]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.3", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no3/", "k": "18", "al": [], "q": "図に示す、アナログ方式の回路計(テスタ)で抵抗値を測定するとき、準備の手順として正しいのはどれか。", "x": "<div>\n      <img loading=\"lazy\" \n        src=\"img/7f3f098925.png\" \n        alt=\"3陸特_無線工学No3_問題18\"  >\n    </div>", "o": ["イ → ア → ウ", "ウ → ア → イ", "ア → イ → ウ", "ウ → イ → ア"], "a": 1, "e": "<b>アナログテスタで抵抗を測る前の基本手順は以下の通り：<br>\n      測定レンジを選ぶ（適切なΩレンジに切り替える）<br>\n      テストリード（テスト棒）を短絡（接触）する<br>\n      ゼロオーム調整（0Ω校正）をする<br>\n      <br>\n      最初にレンジを選ばないと、調整する基準が変わってしまう<br>\n      ゼロオーム調整は、テストリードを短絡して行う必要がある<br></b>", "ee": "Basic steps before measuring resistance with an analog tester:<br>1. Select the measurement range (switch to a suitable Ω range).<br>2. Short the test leads together.<br>3. Do the zero-ohm (0 Ω) adjustment.<br>If you don't select the range first, the reference you adjusted to changes. The zero-ohm adjustment must be done with the test leads shorted.", "eg": false, "eq": "When measuring resistance with the analog circuit tester shown, which preparation order is correct?", "eo": ["イ → ア → ウ", "ウ → ア → イ", "ア → イ → ウ", "ウ → イ → ア"], "v": [4, 59, 322, 61, 330, 331, 442, 443, 329]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.3", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no3/", "k": "19", "al": [], "q": "AM(A3E)通信方式と比べたときの FM(F3E)通信方式の一般的な特徴で、正しいのはどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["占有周波数帯幅が狭い。", "搬送波を抑圧している。", "振幅性の雑音の影響を受けにくい。", "装置の回路構成が簡単である。"], "a": 2, "e": "<b>FM（F3E：周波数変調）の特徴：<br>\n      FM方式では情報を搬送波の「周波数」にのせて送信します。<br>\n      <br>\n      雑音（ノイズ）の多くは「振幅」に現れるため、FMは振幅の変化に強く、ノイズに強いという特長があります。<br></b>", "ee": "FM (F3E, frequency modulation) carries information on the carrier's frequency. Most noise shows up as changes in amplitude, so FM is robust against amplitude changes and therefore resistant to noise.", "eg": false, "eq": "Which is a correct general characteristic of FM (F3E) communication compared with AM (A3E)?", "eo": ["The occupied bandwidth is narrower.", "The carrier is suppressed.", "It is less affected by amplitude noise.", "The circuit configuration of the equipment is simple."], "v": [72, 76, 73, 322, 334, 538, 1, 21, 74, 75, 308, 328, 332, 340, 397, 414, 444]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.3", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no3/", "k": "20", "al": [{"s": "例題集 No.2", "k": "20", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no2/"}], "q": "次の記述は、アナログ通信方式と比べたときのデジタル通信方式の一般的な特徴について述べたものである。誤っているのはどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["雑音の影響を受けにくい。", "ネットワークやコンピュータとの親和性がよい。", "信号処理による遅延がない。", "受信側で誤り訂正を行うことができる。"], "a": 2, "e": "<b>デジタル通信は、以下のような特徴を持ちます：</b>\n      <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/6eacf77afa.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No2_解答20\"  >\n      </div>\n      <b>よって、「信号処理による遅延がない。」が誤りとなります。</b>", "ee": "Digital communication has these characteristics: <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/6eacf77afa.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No2_解答20\"  >\n      </div> Therefore \"there is no delay due to signal processing\" is the incorrect statement.", "eg": false, "eq": "The following describe general characteristics of digital communication compared with analog communication. Which is INCORRECT?", "eo": ["It is less affected by noise.", "It has good compatibility with networks and computers.", "There is no delay due to signal processing.", "Error correction can be performed on the receiving side."], "v": [76, 77, 79, 80, 334, 375, 75, 78, 305, 307, 308, 321, 328, 332, 333, 340, 304]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.3", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no3/", "k": "21", "al": [], "q": "次の記述は、デジタル変調について述べたものである。 (　　　)内に入れるべき字句を下の番号から選べ。<br>\n    <br>\n    QAM は、ベースバンド信号に応じて搬送波の振幅と位相を変化させる方式である。また、16QAMは、1 回の変調(シンボル)で（　　　）ビットの情報を伝送できる。", "x": "", "o": ["２", "４", "６", "８"], "a": 1, "e": "<b>QAM（Quadrature Amplitude Modulation：直交振幅変調）とは：<br>\n      搬送波の「振幅」と「位相」の両方を変化させるデジタル変調方式<br>\n      <br>\n      1つのシンボルで複数ビットをまとめて送れるのが特徴<br>\n\n      16QAMの場合：<br>\n      「16」は16種類のシンボル（状態）があることを意味します。<br>\n      <br>\n      1シンボルで表せるビット数は、以下の式で計算できます：<br>\n      <p>log<sub>2</sub>(16) = 4ビット</p>\n      <br>\n      <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/e6350fce3c.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No2_解答21\"  >\n      </div>", "ee": "QAM (Quadrature Amplitude Modulation) is a digital modulation that varies both the amplitude and the phase of the carrier, so one symbol can carry several bits.<br>In 16QAM, \"16\" means there are 16 symbol states. Bits per symbol = log<sub>2</sub>(16) = 4 bits. <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/e6350fce3c.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No2_解答21\"  >\n      </div>", "eg": false, "eq": "The following describes digital modulation. Choose what fills the blank. QAM varies the carrier's amplitude and phase according to the baseband signal. 16QAM can transmit ( ) bits of information per modulation (symbol).", "eo": [null, null, null, null], "v": [73, 315, 65, 70, 71, 81, 82, 305, 306, 316, 319, 321, 331, 336, 361, 415, 304, 314, 317, 416]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.3", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no3/", "k": "22", "al": [], "q": "次の記述は、デジタル変調について述べたものである。(　　　)内に入れるべき字句を下の番号から選べ。<br>\n  <br>\n  入力信号の「0」又は「1」によって、搬送波の周波数を変化させる方式方式を、(　　　)という。", "x": "", "o": ["ASK", "PSK", "FSK", "QAM"], "a": 2, "e": "<div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/9cefb6c5c6.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No2_解答21\"  >\n      </div>", "ee": "FSK (Frequency Shift Keying) changes the carrier's frequency according to \"0\" or \"1\". ASK changes amplitude, PSK changes phase, and QAM changes both amplitude and phase.<div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/9cefb6c5c6.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No2_解答21\"  >\n      </div>", "eg": true, "eq": "The following describes digital modulation. Choose what fills the blank. The method that changes the carrier frequency according to an input signal of \"0\" or \"1\" is called ( ).", "eo": [null, null, null, null], "v": [465, 42, 73, 315, 65, 305, 306, 313, 316, 319, 321, 331, 361, 304, 314, 317]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.3", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no3/", "k": "23", "al": [], "q": "スーパヘテロダイン受信機の周波数変換部の働きについての記述で、正しいのはどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["受信周波数を音声周波数に変える。", "中間周波数を音声周波数に変える。", "音声周波数を中間周波数に変える。", "受信周波数を中間周波数に変える。"], "a": 3, "e": "<b>スーパヘテロダイン受信機とは：<br>\n      受信した高周波信号（RF）を局部発振器と混合器によって中間周波数（IF）に変換し、その後に増幅・検波・復調する構成の受信機です。<br>\n      <br>\n      周波数変換部の役割：<br>\n      受信周波数（RF）と局部発振周波数（LO）の差（または和）をとることで、<br>\n      一定の中間周波数（IF）に変換しやすくするのが目的。<br>\n      これにより、高性能で選択度・感度に優れた受信が可能になります。</b>", "ee": "A superheterodyne receiver mixes the received RF signal with a local oscillator to convert it to an intermediate frequency (IF), then amplifies, detects and demodulates it.<br>The frequency conversion section takes the difference (or sum) of the received frequency (RF) and the local oscillator frequency (LO) to produce a fixed IF. This gives high performance with good selectivity and sensitivity.", "eg": false, "eq": "Which statement about the function of the frequency conversion section of a superheterodyne receiver is correct?", "eo": ["Converts the received frequency to audio frequency.", "Converts the intermediate frequency to audio frequency.", "Converts audio frequency to the intermediate frequency.", "Converts the received frequency to the intermediate frequency."], "v": [97, 98, 99, 100, 88, 322, 345, 305, 392]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.3", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no3/", "k": "24", "al": [], "q": "FM(F3E)送受信機の操作で、誤っているのはどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["音量調整つまみは、最も聞き易い音量に調整する。", "送信の際、マイクロホンと口の距離は、5～10〔cm〕ぐらいが適当である。", "他局が通話中のとき、プレストークボタンを押し、送信割り込みをしても良い。", "制御器を使用する場合、切換スイッチは、「遠操」にしておく。"], "a": 2, "e": "<b>FM（F3E）送受信機の運用マナーとルール：<br>\n      無線通信では、「聞きながら、相手の通信が終わるのを待つ」という基本的なマナー・ルールがあります。<br>\n      他局が通話中に割り込んで送信すること（送信割り込み）は禁止・または非礼にあたります。<br>\n      特にプレストークボタン（PTT）を押すと即送信状態になるため、誤操作も注意が必要です。<br>\n      </b>", "ee": "Operating etiquette for FM (F3E) transceivers: the basic rule is to listen and wait for the other party's transmission to finish. Cutting in while another station is talking is prohibited (or at least very rude). Pressing the PTT button transmits immediately, so also beware of pressing it by mistake.", "eg": false, "eq": "Which is INCORRECT regarding operation of an FM (F3E) transceiver?", "eo": ["Set the volume knob to the most comfortable listening level.", "When transmitting, 5–10 cm between the microphone and mouth is appropriate.", "When another station is talking, you may press the press-to-talk button and interrupt with a transmission.", "When using a controller, set the selector switch to \"remote operation\" (遠操)."], "v": [90, 135, 500, 125, 505, 63, 132, 133, 134, 250, 318, 320, 333, 376, 393, 424, 502, 503, 504, 506, 467, 501]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.2", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no2/", "k": "13", "al": [], "q": "図に示す回路の端子 ab 間の合成抵抗の値として、正しいのはどれか。", "x": "<div>\n    <img loading=\"lazy\" \n      src=\"img/593b0e2eb6.png\" \n      alt=\"無線工学No2_問題13\"  >\n  </div>", "o": ["50〔kΩ〕", "30〔kΩ〕", "20〔kΩ〕", "10〔kΩ〕"], "a": 3, "e": "<p><b>\n      抵抗𝑅1と𝑅2を並列に接続したときの合成抵抗𝑅合成は以下の式で求めます：\n      </b></p>\n\n      <p>\\( \\frac{1}{R_{\\text{合成}}} = \\frac{1}{R_1} + \\frac{1}{R_2} \\)</p>\n      <p><b>\n      今回の回路では：<br></b></p>\n      <p>\\( R_1 = R_2 = 20\\mathrm{k\\Omega} \\)</p>\n      したがって、<br>\n      <p><b>\n      今回の回路では：<br></b></p>\n      <p>\\(\\frac{1}{R_{\\text{合成}}} = \\frac{1}{20} + \\frac{1}{20} = \\frac{2}{20} = \\frac{1}{10}\\)</p>\n      \n      <p>\\(R_{\\text{合成}} = 10\\,\\mathrm{k\\Omega}\\)</p>", "ee": "For resistors R1 and R2 in parallel, the combined resistance is: \\( \\frac{1}{R_{\\text{total}}} = \\frac{1}{R_1} + \\frac{1}{R_2} \\)<br>In this circuit \\( R_1 = R_2 = 20\\,\\mathrm{k\\Omega} \\), so: \\(\\frac{1}{R_{\\text{total}}} = \\frac{1}{20} + \\frac{1}{20} = \\frac{2}{20} = \\frac{1}{10}\\), giving \\(R_{\\text{total}} = 10\\,\\mathrm{k\\Omega}\\)", "eg": false, "eq": "What is the combined resistance between terminals a and b in the circuit shown?", "eo": [null, null, null, null], "v": [3, 322, 1, 12, 330, 327, 329, 382]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.2", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no2/", "k": "14", "al": [], "q": "図に示す NPN 形トランジスタの図記号において、電極 a の名称はどれか。", "x": "<div>\n    <img loading=\"lazy\" \n      src=\"img/39b614b58f.png\" \n      alt=\"無線工学No2_問題14\"  >\n  </div>", "o": ["エミッタ", "ベース", "コレクタ", "ゲート"], "a": 2, "e": "<div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/ccdc41e4f0.png\" \n          alt=\"接合型トランジスタと接合型FET\"  >\n      </div>\n      <br>\n      <b>aに該当する部分は、コレクタになります。</b>", "ee": "<div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/ccdc41e4f0.png\" \n          alt=\"接合型トランジスタと接合型FET\"  >\n      </div> The part marked a is the collector.", "eg": false, "eq": "In the NPN transistor symbol shown, what is the name of electrode a?", "eo": ["Emitter", "Base", "Collector", "Gate"], "v": [120, 22, 119, 330, 329, 507]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.2", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no2/", "k": "15", "al": [], "q": "超短波(VHF)帯の周波数を利用する送受信設備において、装置とアンテナを接続する給電線として、通常使用されるものはどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["同軸ケーブル", "導波管線路", "平行２線式線路", "LAN ケーブル"], "a": 0, "e": "<b>超短波（VHF）帯とは：<br>\n      周波数範囲：約30MHz～300MHz<br>\n      <br>\n      無線通信、テレビ放送、FMラジオなどで使われます。<br></b>\n      <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/5563aee28e.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No2_解答15\"  >\n      </div>", "ee": "The VHF band is roughly 30 MHz to 300 MHz, used for radio communication, TV broadcasting, FM radio, etc. <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/5563aee28e.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No2_解答15\"  >\n      </div>", "eg": false, "eq": "In transmitting/receiving equipment using VHF frequencies, which feed line is normally used to connect the equipment and antenna?", "eo": ["Coaxial cable", "Waveguide line", "Parallel two-wire line", "LAN cable"], "v": [91, 28, 42, 121, 123, 122, 124, 320, 397, 448, 508, 509, 510, 539, 412]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.2", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no2/", "k": "16", "al": [], "q": "次の記述において 内に入れるべき字句の正しい組合せを下の番号から選べ。<br>\n\n    電波の伝搬速度は、光の速さと同じで１秒間に３ × （A）メートルである。また、同一波形が１秒間に繰り返される回数を（B）という。", "x": "", "o": ["(A) 10<sup>8</sup>, (B) 周波数", "(A) 10<sup>8</sup>, (B) 周期", "(A) 10<sup>10</sup>, (B) 周波数", "(A) 10<sup>10</sup>, (B) 周期"], "a": 0, "e": "<b>この波の山と山あるいは谷と谷の間の時間を周期(単位：秒[sec])と言います。また、1秒間の周期の数を周波数といい、単位をヘルツ[Hz]で表現します。</b>\n      <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/4214f92ac6.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No2_解答16\"  >\n      </div>", "ee": "The time between two peaks (or two troughs) of a wave is the period (unit: seconds). The number of periods in one second is the frequency, measured in hertz (Hz). <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/4214f92ac6.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No2_解答16\"  >\n      </div>", "eg": false, "eq": "Choose the correct combination for the blanks. Radio waves propagate at the speed of light: 3 × (A) meters per second. The number of times the same waveform repeats in one second is called (B).", "eo": ["(A) 10<sup>8</sup>, (B) frequency", "(A) 10<sup>8</sup>, (B) period", "(A) 10<sup>10</sup>, (B) frequency", "(A) 10<sup>10</sup>, (B) period"], "v": [39, 440, 42, 315, 322, 339, 40, 41, 138, 305, 306, 316, 319, 374, 396, 438, 439, 441, 304, 314, 317, 437]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.2", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no2/", "k": "17", "al": [{"s": "過去問 令和3年10月", "k": "17", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_musen_0310/"}], "q": "蓄電池のアンペア時〔Ah〕は、何を表すか。", "x": "", "o": ["定格電流", "起電力", "内部抵抗", "容量"], "a": 3, "e": "<b>アンペア時（Ah：Ampere-hour）は、蓄電池がどれだけの電流をどれだけの時間流せるかを表すための指標です。<br>\n      <br>\n      たとえば：<br>\n      10Ahのバッテリーとは、1Aの電流を10時間流せる能力があるという意味になります。</b>", "ee": "Ampere-hours (Ah) show how much current a battery can supply for how long. For example, a 10 Ah battery can supply 1 A for 10 hours.", "eg": false, "eq": "What does the ampere-hour [Ah] rating of a storage battery represent?", "eo": ["Rated current", "Electromotive force", "Internal resistance", "Capacity"], "v": [45, 48, 43, 47, 49, 371, 389, 431]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.2", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no2/", "k": "18", "al": [], "q": "次の記述において(　　　)内に入れるべき字句の正しい組合せを下の番号から選べ。<br>\n  アナログ方式の回路計(テスタ)を用いて直流電圧を測定しようとするときは、切替つまみを測定しようとする電圧の値よりやや（A）の値の（B）レンジにする。", "x": "", "o": ["(A) 小さめ, (B) AC VOLTS", "(A) 小さめ, (B) DC VOLTS", "(A) 大きめ, (B) AC VOLTS", "(A) 大きめ, (B) DC VOLTS"], "a": 3, "e": "<b>アナログテスタで直流電圧（DC:Direct Current）を測定する場合：<br>\n      B：「DC VOLTS」<br>\n      　→ 直流電圧を測るには「DC VOLTS」レンジを選びます。<br>\n      <br>\n      A：「大きめ」<br>\n      　→ 測定対象の電圧が不明なときや、誤って大きな電圧が加わる可能性があるとき、メーターの振り切れ（針が端まで振れる）を防ぐために、最初は大きめのレンジから始めるのが安全です。<br>\n      　確認後、適切なレンジに下げて精度を上げます。<br>\n      </b>", "ee": "When measuring DC voltage with an analog tester:<br>B: \"DC VOLTS\" – choose the DC VOLTS range for direct-current voltage.<br>A: \"larger\" – when the voltage is unknown or a high voltage could be applied by mistake, start with a larger range to avoid pinning the needle. Then step down to a suitable range for better accuracy.", "eg": false, "eq": "Choose the correct combination for the blanks. When measuring DC voltage with an analog circuit tester, set the selector knob to the (B) range with a value slightly (A) than the voltage to be measured.", "eo": ["(A) smaller, (B) AC VOLTS", "(A) smaller, (B) DC VOLTS", "(A) larger, (B) AC VOLTS", "(A) larger, (B) DC VOLTS"], "v": [59, 315, 322, 339, 363, 365, 7, 9, 61, 305, 306, 316, 319, 331, 398, 434, 304, 314, 317, 327]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.2", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no2/", "k": "19", "al": [], "q": "AM(A3E)送信機において、音声信号で変調された搬送波はどのようになっているか。", "x": "", "o": ["断続している。", "周波数が変化している。", "振幅が変化している。", "振幅、周波数ともに変化しない。"], "a": 2, "e": "<b>AM（Amplitude Modulation、振幅変調）とは：<br>\n      音声信号などの情報を、搬送波の「振幅」に乗せる方式です。<br>\n      <br>\n      A3Eは、音声信号によるAM（振幅変調）の代表的な形式で、搬送波＋両側波帯（USBとLSB）で構成されます。<br></b>\n      <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/81a32e7334.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No2_解答19\"  >\n      </div>", "ee": "AM (amplitude modulation) puts the information, such as a voice signal, on the carrier's amplitude. A3E is the typical voice AM format, made up of the carrier plus both sidebands (USB and LSB). <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/81a32e7334.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No2_解答19\"  >\n      </div>", "eg": false, "eq": "In an AM (A3E) transmitter, what happens to a carrier modulated by a voice signal?", "eo": ["It is intermittent (on/off).", "Its frequency changes.", "Its amplitude changes.", "Neither amplitude nor frequency changes."], "v": [466, 42, 73, 89, 65, 70, 136, 361]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.2", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no2/", "k": "21", "al": [], "q": "次の記述は、多元接続方式について述べたものである。 (　　　)内に入れるべき字句を下の番号から選べ。<br>\n    <br>\n   TDMA は、一つの周波数を共有し、個々のユーザに使用チャネルとして(　　　)を個別に割り当てる方式であり、チャネルとチャネルの間にガードタイムを設けている。", "x": "", "o": ["極めて短い時間(タイムスロット)", "拡散符号", "変調方式", "周波数"], "a": 0, "e": "<b>TDMA（Time Division Multiple Access：時分割多元接続方式）とは：<br>\n      1つの周波数帯域を、複数のユーザーが時間的に交代で使う方式です。<br>\n      <br>\n      各ユーザーには「タイムスロット（極めて短い時間）」が割り当てられ、その間だけ送受信を行います。<br>\n      <br>\n      ユーザー間の信号干渉を防ぐために「ガードタイム」が設けられます。<br></b>\n      <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/17ba999532.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No2_解答21\"  >\n      </div>", "ee": "TDMA (Time Division Multiple Access) lets several users share one frequency band by taking turns in time. Each user gets a time slot (a very short period of time) and transmits/receives only during it. Guard time is placed between slots to prevent interference between users. <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/17ba999532.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No2_解答21\"  >\n      </div>", "eg": false, "eq": "The following describes multiple access methods. Choose what fills the blank. TDMA shares one frequency and individually assigns ( ) to each user as their channel, with guard time between channels.", "eo": ["Very short periods of time (time slots)", "Spreading codes", "Modulation methods", "Frequencies"], "v": [86, 69, 83, 84, 42, 315, 470, 85, 87, 305, 306, 316, 319, 320, 321, 331, 468, 469, 471, 472, 511, 304, 314, 317, 382]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.2", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no2/", "k": "22", "al": [], "q": "図は、デジタル無線受信装置の概念図例を示したものである。デジタル信号とアナログ信号を変換するする装置はどれか。<br>\n  <div>\n    <img loading=\"lazy\" \n      src=\"img/dc1ec81dd9.png\" \n      alt=\"無線工学No2_問題22\"  >\n  </div>", "x": "", "o": ["周波数変換器", "IDC 回路", "AFC 回路", "D / A 変換器"], "a": 3, "e": "<b>図の中で、受信機から出力されたデジタル信号が、スピーカで音声として再生される前に「アナログ信号」に変換されています。<br>\n      この変換（デジタル → アナログ）を行う装置をD/A変換器（Digital to Analog Converter）といいます。</b>\n      <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/aefd2229fe.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No2_解答22\"  >\n      </div>", "ee": "In the diagram, the digital signal from the receiver is converted to an analog signal before the speaker plays it as sound. The device that does this digital → analog conversion is a D/A converter (Digital-to-Analog Converter). <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/aefd2229fe.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No2_解答22\"  >\n      </div>", "eg": false, "eq": "The figure is an example conceptual diagram of a digital radio receiver. Which device converts between digital and analog signals?", "eo": ["Frequency converter", "IDC circuit (instantaneous deviation control)", "AFC circuit (automatic frequency control)", "D/A converter"], "v": [96, 92, 94, 95, 1, 330, 336, 391, 397, 512, 329, 417]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.2", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no2/", "k": "23", "al": [], "q": "スーパヘテロダイン受信機の近接周波数に対する選択度特性に最も影響を与えるものはどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["検波器", "高周波増幅器", "中間周波増幅器", "周波数変換器"], "a": 2, "e": "<b>選択度とは、「目的の信号と近接する妨害波をどれだけ分離できるか」の指標。<br>\n      スーパヘテロダイン方式では、中間周波（IF）段で最も鋭いフィルタリングが行われる。<br>\n      IFは固定周波数なので、高品質なフィルタ設計が可能。<br>\n      これにより、近接周波数との分離性能（＝選択度）が決まる。</b>", "ee": "Selectivity is how well a receiver separates the wanted signal from nearby interfering signals. In a superheterodyne receiver the sharpest filtering happens in the IF stage. Because the IF is a fixed frequency, high-quality filters can be designed for it, and these determine the separation from adjacent frequencies (the selectivity).", "eg": false, "eq": "In a superheterodyne receiver, what most affects selectivity against adjacent frequencies?", "eo": ["Detector", "RF (high-frequency) amplifier", "IF (intermediate-frequency) amplifier", "Frequency converter"], "v": [102, 96, 103, 109, 88, 111, 115, 344, 380, 328, 376, 445]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.2", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no2/", "k": "24", "al": [], "q": "無線送受信機の制御器(コントロールパネル)は、一般にどのような目的で使用されるか。", "x": "", "o": ["送受信機を離れたところから操作する。", "アンテナと給電線のインピーダンス整合を調整する。", "停電などの際、送受信機へ供給される電力の瞬断をなくす。", "送受信機から発射されるスプリアスを低下させる。"], "a": 0, "e": "<b>制御器（コントロールパネル）は、下記の操作をオペレーションルームや管制卓などから行えるようにする装置です。：<br>\n      　- 無線送受信機の遠隔操作<br>\n      　- 送受信機などの電源 ON/OFF<br>\n      　- 周波数の設定<br>\n      　- 送受信切り替え<br></b>", "ee": "A controller (control panel) lets these operations be done from an operations room or control desk:<br>– Remote operation of the transceiver<br>– Power ON/OFF of the transceiver, etc.<br>– Frequency setting<br>– Switching between transmit and receive", "eg": false, "eq": "For what purpose is the controller (control panel) of a radio transceiver generally used?", "eo": ["To operate the transceiver from a distant location.", "To adjust impedance matching between the antenna and feed line.", "To eliminate momentary power interruptions to the transceiver during outages.", "To reduce spurious emissions from the transceiver."], "v": [90, 121, 125, 6, 63, 126, 127, 128, 129, 131, 250, 280, 320, 335, 391, 395, 513, 467]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.1", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no1/", "k": "14", "al": [], "q": "接合形トランジスタの電極と電界効果トランジスタ(FET)の電極の組合せで、その働きが対応しているのはどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["ベース / ドレイン", "ベース / ゲート", "エミッタ / ドレイン", "コレクタ / ソース"], "a": 1, "e": "<div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/ccdc41e4f0.png\" \n          alt=\"接合型トランジスタと接合型FET\"  >\n      </div>\n      <br>\n      <b>トランジスタとFETは、ベースに対応する端子が「ゲート」、コレクタに対応する端子が「ドレイン」、エミッタに対応する端子が「ソース」と呼ばれます。</b>", "ee": "<div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/ccdc41e4f0.png\" \n          alt=\"接合型トランジスタと接合型FET\"  >\n      </div> Between a transistor and an FET: the terminal corresponding to the base is the gate, the collector corresponds to the drain, and the emitter corresponds to the source.", "eg": false, "eq": "Which pairing of a junction transistor electrode with a field-effect transistor (FET) electrode has corresponding functions?", "eo": ["Base / Drain", "Base / Gate", "Emitter / Drain", "Collector / Source"], "v": [117, 118, 339, 119, 392, 436]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.1", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no1/", "k": "15", "al": [], "q": "図は、三素子八木・宇田アンテナ(八木アンテナ)の構成を示したものである。各素子の名称の組合せで、正しいのはどれか。次のうちから選べ。ただし、A、B、C の長さは、A ＜ B ＜ C の関係があるものとする。", "x": "<div>\n    <img loading=\"lazy\" \n      src=\"img/66be29032a.png\" \n      alt=\"八木アンテナ\"  >\n  </div>", "o": ["A:反射器 B:導波器 C:放射器", "A:反射器 B:放射器 C:導波器", "A:導波器 B:反射器 C:放射器", "A:導波器 B:放射器 C:反射器"], "a": 3, "e": "<div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/afc3b9ffc5.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No1_解答15\"  >\n      </div>", "ee": "In a Yagi antenna the three elements have different lengths: the director (導波器) is the shortest and sits at the front, the radiator (放射器) is about λ/2 and is fed with the signal, and the reflector (反射器) is the longest and sits at the back. With A &lt; B &lt; C: A = director, B = radiator, C = reflector.<div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/afc3b9ffc5.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No1_解答15\"  >\n      </div>", "eg": true, "eq": "The figure shows the structure of a three-element Yagi-Uda antenna (Yagi antenna). Which combination of element names is correct? Assume the lengths satisfy A < B < C.", "eo": ["A: reflector, B: director, C: radiator", "A: reflector, B: radiator, C: director", "A: director, B: reflector, C: radiator", "A: director, B: radiator, C: reflector"], "v": [23, 24, 25, 322, 339, 20, 21, 22, 306, 330, 384, 385, 386, 430, 304, 329, 428, 429]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.1", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no1/", "k": "16", "al": [], "q": "短波(HF)の伝わり方と比べたときの超短波(VHF)の伝わり方の記述で、最も適切なものはどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["見通し距離外の通信に適する。", "太陽の紫外線による影響を受ける。", "昼間と夜間では、電波の伝わり方が異なる。", "通常、電離層を突き抜けてしまう。"], "a": 3, "e": "", "ee": "Unlike HF, which is reflected by the ionosphere and can travel beyond the horizon, VHF normally passes straight through the ionosphere. VHF is therefore used for line-of-sight communication, and it isn't affected by day/night ionosphere changes or solar UV the way HF is.", "eg": true, "eq": "Which statement best describes how VHF propagates compared with HF?", "eo": ["It is suitable for communication beyond line of sight.", "It is affected by the sun's ultraviolet rays.", "Propagation differs between day and night.", "It normally passes through the ionosphere."], "v": [31, 518, 540, 28, 37, 38, 308, 474, 517, 29, 138, 305, 328, 332, 349, 376, 421, 509, 514, 515, 516, 473]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.1", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no1/", "k": "17", "al": [], "q": "機器に用いる電源ヒューズの電流値は、機器の規格電流に比べて、どのような値のものが最も適切か。", "x": "", "o": ["少し小さい値", "十分小さい値", "少し大きい値", "十分大きい値"], "a": 2, "e": "<b>電源ヒューズの電流値は、機器の規格電流に比べて、少し大きめのものが適切です。<br>\n      少し小さい値や十分小さい値だと、正常な電流でもヒューズが切れてしまう恐れがあります。<br>\n      十分大きい値だと、異常時でもヒューズが切れず、機器を保護できません。</b>\n      <br>", "ee": "The fuse rating should be slightly larger than the equipment's rated current. With a slightly or much smaller value, the fuse may blow even under normal current. With a much larger value, the fuse won't blow in a fault and can't protect the equipment.", "eg": false, "eq": "Compared with the equipment's rated current, what current value is most appropriate for the equipment's power fuse?", "eo": ["Slightly smaller value", "Much smaller value", "Slightly larger value", "Much larger value"], "v": [46, 364, 366, 398, 8, 130, 332, 351, 376, 404, 421, 519, 327]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.1", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no1/", "k": "18", "al": [], "q": "抵抗 R に流れる電流を測定するときの電流計 A のつなぎ方を示す接続図として、正しいのはどれか。", "x": "<div>\n      <img loading=\"lazy\" \n        src=\"img/f446bc4363.png\" \n        alt=\"接合型トランジスタと接合型FET\"  >\n    </div>", "o": ["1", "2", "3", "4"], "a": 1, "e": "<b>電流計は、電流が流れる回路に対して直列に接続します。</b>", "ee": "An ammeter is connected in series with the circuit whose current is being measured.", "eg": false, "eq": "Which connection diagram correctly shows how to connect ammeter A to measure the current flowing through resistor R?", "eo": [null, null, null, null], "v": [541, 60, 64, 322, 411, 2, 8, 61, 330]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.1", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no1/", "k": "19", "al": [], "q": "振幅変調(A3E)波と比べたときの周波数変調（F3E）波の占有周波数帯幅の一般的な特徴はどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["広い", "狭い", "同じ", "半分"], "a": 0, "e": "<b>周波数変調は、周波数を用いて変調しているので、振幅変調と比較して周波数帯域は広くなります。</b>", "ee": "Frequency modulation modulates using frequency, so its bandwidth is wider than that of amplitude modulation.", "eg": false, "eq": "Compared with an amplitude-modulated (A3E) wave, what is the general characteristic of the occupied bandwidth of a frequency-modulated (F3E) wave?", "eo": ["Wider", "Narrower", "The same", "Half"], "v": [72, 67, 66, 334, 332, 340, 374, 413, 414, 432, 390]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.1", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no1/", "k": "20", "al": [], "q": "次の記述は、アナログ通信方式と比べたときのデジタル通信方式の一般的な特徴について述べたものである。誤っているのはどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["ネットワークやコンピュータとの親和性がよい。", "信号処理による遅延が生じる。", "雑音の影響を受けやすい。", "受信側で誤り訂正を行うことができる。"], "a": 2, "e": "<b>デジタル変調は、アナログ変調と比べて雑音の影響を受けにくいです。</b>", "ee": "Digital modulation is less affected by noise than analog modulation.", "eg": false, "eq": "The following describe general characteristics of digital communication compared with analog communication. Which is INCORRECT?", "eo": ["It has good compatibility with networks and computers.", "Delay occurs due to signal processing.", "It is easily affected by noise.", "Error correction can be performed on the receiving side."], "v": [76, 77, 79, 80, 334, 360, 375, 75, 78, 305, 307, 308, 321, 328, 332, 333, 340, 304]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.1", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no1/", "k": "21", "al": [], "q": "次の記述は、多元接続方式について述べたものである。 (　　　)内に入れるべき字句を下の番号から選べ。<br>\n    <br>\n    FDMA は、個々のユーザに使用チャネルとして(　　　)を個別に割り当てる方式であり、チャネルとチャネルの間にガードバンドを設けている。", "x": "", "o": ["極めて短い時間", "拡散符号", "変調方式", "周波数"], "a": 3, "e": "<b>FDMA(Frequency Division Multiple Access)は、周波数で多元接続する方式です。</b>", "ee": "FDMA (Frequency Division Multiple Access) provides multiple access by dividing up frequencies.", "eg": false, "eq": "The following describes multiple access methods. Choose what fills the blank. FDMA individually assigns ( ) to each user as their channel, with a guard band between channels.", "eo": ["Very short periods of time", "Spreading codes", "Modulation methods", "Frequencies"], "v": [86, 69, 83, 84, 42, 315, 470, 85, 305, 306, 316, 319, 320, 321, 331, 468, 469, 471, 472, 304, 314, 317, 382]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.1", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no1/", "k": "22", "al": [], "q": "次の記述は、デジタル変調について述べたものである。(　　　)内に入れるべき字句を下の番号から選べ。<br>\n  <br>\n  入力信号の「0」又は「1」によって、搬送波の位相のみを変化させる方式を、(　　　)という。", "x": "", "o": ["ASK", "FSK", "QAM", "PSK"], "a": 3, "e": "<b>PSK（Phase Shift Keying：位相偏移変調）は、搬送波の位相を変化させてデジタルデータ（「0」や「1」）を表す変調方式です。<br></b>\n      <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/5e802fc4a7.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No1_解答22\"  >\n      </div>", "ee": "PSK (Phase Shift Keying) represents digital data (\"0\" and \"1\") by changing the phase of the carrier. <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/5e802fc4a7.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No1_解答22\"  >\n      </div>", "eg": false, "eq": "The following describes digital modulation. Choose what fills the blank. The method that changes only the carrier phase according to an input signal of \"0\" or \"1\" is called ( ).", "eo": [null, null, null, null], "v": [465, 73, 315, 65, 71, 305, 306, 313, 316, 319, 321, 331, 361, 304, 314, 317]}, {"c": "tech", "s": "例題集 No.1", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_musen_exercise_no1/", "k": "23", "al": [], "q": "次の記述は、受信機の性能のうち何について述べたものか。<br>\n  <br>\n  送信された信号を受信し、受信機の出力側で元の信号がどれだけ忠実に再現できるかという能力を表す。", "x": "", "o": ["忠実度", "安定度", "選択度", "感度"], "a": 0, "e": "<div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/84b6f337ad.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No1_解答23\"  >\n      </div>", "ee": "Fidelity (忠実度) is the ability to faithfully reproduce the original signal at the receiver output. Sensitivity is the ability to receive weak signals, selectivity is separating the wanted signal from nearby ones, and stability is holding frequency and gain steady.<div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/84b6f337ad.png\" \n          alt=\"無線工学No1_解答23\"  >\n      </div>", "eg": true, "eq": "Which receiver performance characteristic does this describe? The ability to faithfully reproduce the original signal at the receiver output after receiving the transmitted signal.", "eo": ["Fidelity", "Stability", "Selectivity", "Sensitivity"], "v": [88, 111, 112, 113, 520, 114, 116, 305, 321, 336, 371, 389, 424, 425, 522, 523, 524, 304, 521]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.3", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no3/", "k": "1", "al": [], "q": "無線局の免許を与えられないことがある者はどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["電波法に規定する罪を犯し罰金以上の刑に処せられ、その執行を終わった日から２年を経過しない者", "刑法に規定する罪を犯し拘禁刑に処せられ、その執行を終わった日から２年を経過しない者", "無線局の免許の取消しを受け、その取消しの日から５年を経過しない者", "無線局を廃止し、その廃止の日から２年を経過しない者"], "a": 0, "e": "<b>電波法又は放送法に規定する罪を犯し罰金以上の刑に処せられ、その執行を終わり、又はその執行を受けることがなくなった日から2年を経過しない者には、無線局の免許を与えないことができます(電波法 第5条)</b>", "ee": "A station license may be refused to a person who committed a crime under the Radio Act or Broadcast Act, was sentenced to a fine or heavier, and 2 years have not passed since the sentence was completed or ceased to apply. (Radio Act, Art. 5)", "eg": false, "eq": "Who may be refused a radio station license?", "eo": ["A person who committed a crime under the Radio Act, was sentenced to a fine or heavier, and 2 years have not passed since the sentence was completed", "A person who committed a crime under the Penal Code, was sentenced to imprisonment, and 2 years have not passed since the sentence was completed", "A person whose station license was revoked, and 5 years have not passed since the revocation", "A person who closed a radio station, and 2 years have not passed since the closure"], "v": [220, 137, 139, 201, 219, 379, 145, 160, 208, 214, 216, 217, 221, 222, 308, 341, 344, 215, 218, 309, 311, 535]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.3", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no3/", "k": "2", "al": [], "q": "無線局の免許人は、電波の型式及び周波数の指定の変更を受けようとするときは、どうしなければならないか。", "x": "", "o": ["総務大臣に電波の型式及び周波数の指定の変更を届け出る。", "あらかじめ総務大臣の指示を受ける。", "総務大臣に電波の型式及び周波数の指定の変更を申請する。", "免許状を総務大臣に提出し、訂正を受ける。"], "a": 2, "e": "<b>\n    総務大臣は、免許人又は第八条の予備免許を受けた者が識別信号、電波の型式、周波数、空中線電力又は運用許容時間の指定の変更を申請した場合において、混信の除去その他特に必要があると認めるときは、その指定を変更することができる。(電波法 第19条)<br>\n    <br>\n    1番：「届け出」ではなく「申請」が必要です。<br>\n      <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/70c80adae9.png\" \n          alt=\"3陸特_法規No3_問題1\"  >\n      </div>\n    2番：法律上「指示を受ける」必要はありません。<br>\n    4番：免許状の訂正は変更後に行われますが、先に申請して変更の許可を得る必要があります。<br></b>", "ee": "\"When a licensee (or holder of a provisional license under Art. 8) applies for a change to the designated call sign, emission type, frequency, antenna power or permitted operating hours, the Minister may change the designation if it is especially necessary, e.g. to remove interference.\" (Radio Act, Art. 19)<br>Choice \"notify\": wrong, an application is required, not a notification. <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/70c80adae9.png\" \n          alt=\"3陸特_法規No3_問題1\"  >\n      </div><br>Choice \"obtain instructions\": the law does not require receiving instructions.<br>Choice \"submit the license for correction\": the correction happens after the change; you must first apply and get the change approved.", "eg": false, "eq": "What must a licensee do to have the designated emission type and frequency changed?", "eo": ["Notify the Minister of the change in designated emission type and frequency.", "Obtain the Minister's instructions in advance.", "Apply to the Minister for a change in designated emission type and frequency.", "Submit the license to the Minister and have it corrected."], "v": [158, 162, 42, 139, 146, 147, 308, 138, 156, 165, 175, 188, 197, 296, 310, 409]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.3", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no3/", "k": "3", "al": [], "q": "電波の主搬送波の変調の型式が角度変調で周波数変調のもの、主搬送波を変調する信号の性質がアナログ信号である単一チャネルのものであって、伝送情報の型式が電話（音響の放送を含む。）の電波の型式を表示する記号はどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["Ａ３Ｅ", "Ｆ３Ｅ", "Ｆ７Ｅ", "Ｆ８Ｅ"], "a": 1, "e": "<div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/87bb210ce6.png\" \n          alt=\"技術操作の操作範囲\"  >\n      </div>", "ee": "Emission designation: F = frequency modulation (angle modulation); 3 = a single channel carrying an analog signal; E = telephony (including sound broadcasting). So the symbol is F3E. (A3E would be amplitude modulation.)<div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/87bb210ce6.png\" \n          alt=\"技術操作の操作範囲\"  >\n      </div>", "eg": true, "eq": "Which symbol designates the emission type where the main carrier is angle-modulated by frequency modulation, the modulating signal is a single analog channel, and the information transmitted is telephony (including sound broadcasting)?", "eo": [null, null, null, null], "v": [67, 189, 190, 192, 65, 138, 188, 191, 193, 194, 195, 196, 336, 410, 453, 454]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.3", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no3/", "k": "4", "al": [], "q": "総務大臣が無線従事者の免許を与えないことができる者はどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["無線従事者の免許を取り消され、取消しの日から２年を経過しない者", "刑法に規定する罪を犯し罰金以上の刑に処せられ、その執行を終わり、又はその執行を受けることがなくなった日から２年を経過しない者", "日本の国籍を有しない者", "無線従事者の免許を取り消され、取消しの日から５年を経過しない者"], "a": 0, "e": "<b>\n      <br>次のいずれかに該当する者に対しては、無線従事者の免許を与えないことができる。\n      <br>・電波法の罪を犯し罰金以上の刑に処せられ、その執行を終わり、又はその執行を受けることがなくなつた日から二年を経過しない者\n      <br>・無線従事者の免許を取り消され、取消しの日から二年を経過しない者\n      <br>・著しく心身に欠陥があつて無線従事者たるに適しない者\n      </b>", "ee": "The Minister may refuse a radio operator license to:<br>• A person who committed a Radio Act crime and was sentenced to a fine or heavier, until 2 years have passed since the sentence was completed or ceased to apply<br>• A person whose radio operator license was revoked, until 2 years have passed since the revocation<br>• A person with a serious mental or physical impairment making them unfit to be a radio operator", "eg": false, "eq": "To whom may the Minister refuse to grant a radio operator license?", "eo": ["A person whose radio operator license was revoked, and 2 years have not passed since the revocation", "A person who committed a crime under the Penal Code, was sentenced to a fine or heavier, and for whom 2 years have not passed since the sentence was completed or ceased to apply", "A person who does not have Japanese nationality", "A person whose radio operator license was revoked, and 5 years have not passed since the revocation"], "v": [141, 158, 202, 220, 201, 308, 145, 160, 214, 216, 217, 221, 222, 223, 313, 338, 341, 344, 358, 379, 215, 218, 309, 311, 535]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.3", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no3/", "k": "5", "al": [], "q": "第三級陸上特殊無線技士の資格を有する者の無線設備の操作の対象となる「陸上の無線局」に該当するものはどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["基地局", "海岸局", "基幹放送局", "航空局"], "a": 0, "e": "<b>陸上の無線局とは、海岸局、海岸地球局、船舶局、船舶地球局、航空局、航空地球局、航空機局、航空機地球局、無線航行局及び基幹放送局<span>以外</span>の無線局をいう。</b><br>", "ee": "\"Land stations\" means radio stations other than coast stations, coast earth stations, ship stations, ship earth stations, aeronautical stations, aeronautical earth stations, aircraft stations, aircraft earth stations, radionavigation stations and core broadcasting stations.", "eg": false, "eq": "Which qualifies as a \"land station\" whose equipment a 3rd Class Land Special Radio Operator may operate?", "eo": ["Base station", "Coast station", "Core broadcasting station", "Aeronautical station"], "v": [144, 243, 140, 139, 240, 241, 242, 338, 227, 236, 250, 354, 525, 309]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.3", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no3/", "k": "6", "al": [], "q": "無線従事者は、免許証を失ったためにその再交付を受けた後、失った免許証を発見したときはどうしなければならないか。", "x": "", "o": ["速やかに発見した免許証を廃棄する。", "発見した日から１０日以内に発見した免許証を総務大臣に返納する。", "発見した日から１０日以内にその旨を総務大臣に届け出る。", "発見した日から１０日以内に再交付を受けた免許証を総務大臣に返納する。"], "a": 1, "e": "<b>免許証の再交付を受けた後、失った免許証を発見したときは、発見した日から10日以内にその免許証を総務大臣又は総合通信局長に返納しなければならない。(無線従事者規則 第51条)</b><br>", "ee": "After a reissue, if the lost license card is found, it must be returned to the Minister (or the Regional Bureau Director) within 10 days of finding it. (Radio Operator Regulations, Art. 51)", "eg": false, "eq": "After a radio operator lost their license card and received a reissue, what must they do if they find the lost card?", "eo": ["Promptly destroy the found card.", "Return the found card to the Minister within 10 days of finding it.", "Notify the Minister of the fact within 10 days of finding it.", "Return the reissued card to the Minister within 10 days of finding the old one."], "v": [141, 158, 162, 167, 148, 151, 152, 276, 277, 308, 325, 343, 311, 312, 324]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.3", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no3/", "k": "7", "al": [], "q": "一般通信方法における無線通信の原則として無線局運用規則に定める事項に該当するものはどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["無線通信は、長時間継続して行ってはならない。", "無線通信は、正確に行うものとし、通信上の誤りを知ったときは、通報の送信終了後一括して訂正しなければならない。", "無線通信に使用する用語は、できる限り簡潔でなければならない。", "無線通信を行う場合においては、暗語を使用してはならない。"], "a": 2, "e": "<b>無線通信に使用する用語は、できる限り簡潔でなければならない。(無線従事者規則 第10条)</b><br>", "ee": "Terms used in radio communication must be as concise as possible. (Radio Station Operation Regulations, Art. 10)", "eg": false, "eq": "Which is a principle of radio communication in general communication methods specified in the Radio Station Operation Regulations?", "eo": ["Radio communication must not be carried on continuously for long periods.", "Radio communication must be accurate; when an error is noticed, it must be corrected all at once after the message transmission ends.", "Terms used in radio communication must be as concise as possible.", "Code words must not be used in radio communication."], "v": [293, 456, 143, 323, 457, 462, 290, 294, 295, 296, 297, 298, 307, 318, 320, 333, 354, 381, 424, 458, 459, 460, 461, 463, 464, 324]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.3", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no3/", "k": "8", "al": [], "q": "無線局の臨時検査（電波法第７３条第５項の検査）が行われることがあるのはどの場合か。", "x": "", "o": ["総務大臣から臨時に電波の発射の停止を命じられたとき。", "無線局の再免許の申請をし、総務大臣から免許が与えられたとき。", "無線従事者を選任したとき。", "無線設備の変更の工事を行ったとき。"], "a": 0, "e": "", "ee": "An extraordinary inspection (Art. 73, Para. 5) may be carried out when, for example, the Minister has ordered a station to temporarily stop emitting radio waves because its wave quality did not conform (Art. 72).", "eg": true, "eq": "In which case may an extraordinary inspection of a station (Radio Act Art. 73, Para. 5) be conducted?", "eo": ["When the Minister has ordered a temporary stop to radio emissions.", "When a license renewal was applied for and granted by the Minister.", "When a radio operator has been appointed.", "When changes (construction work) were made to the radio equipment."], "v": [141, 140, 158, 173, 137, 139, 149, 131, 138, 145, 156, 169, 172, 174, 175, 176, 203, 307, 318, 344, 353, 406, 407, 408]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.3", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no3/", "k": "9", "al": [], "q": "無線局の免許人は、電波法の規定に違反して運用した無線局を認めたときは、どうしなければならないか。", "x": "", "o": ["総務省令で定める手続により、総務大臣に報告する。", "その無線局の電波の発射を停止させる。", "その無線局の免許人にその旨を通知する。", "その無線局の免許人を告発する。"], "a": 0, "e": "<b>無線局の免許人等は、電波法の規定に違反して運用されていることを認めたときは、総務省令で定める手続により、総務大臣に報告しなければならない。(電波法 第80条)", "ee": "When a licensee finds a station being operated in violation of the Radio Act, they must report it to the Minister following the procedure set by MIC ordinance. (Radio Act, Art. 80)", "eg": false, "eq": "What must a licensee do upon recognizing a station operating in violation of the Radio Act?", "eo": ["Report to the Minister following the procedure set by MIC ordinance.", "Make that station stop emitting radio waves.", "Notify that station's licensee.", "File a criminal complaint against that station's licensee."], "v": [158, 159, 137, 139, 146, 323, 131, 138, 160, 163, 199, 203, 210, 299, 300, 302, 378, 312]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.3", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no3/", "k": "10", "al": [], "q": "無線従事者が電波法又は電波法に基づく命令に違反したときに総務大臣から受けることがある処分はどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["期間を定めて行う無線設備の操作範囲の制限", "６箇月間の業務の従事の停止", "その業務に従事する無線局の運用の停止", "無線従事者の免許の取消し"], "a": 3, "e": "", "ee": "For a radio operator who violates the Radio Act, the Minister may revoke the license or suspend them from duties for up to 3 months (not 6 months). Revocation is the only valid choice. (Radio Act, Art. 79)", "eg": true, "eq": "What penalty may a radio operator receive from the Minister for violating the Radio Act or orders based on it?", "eo": ["Restriction of the scope of equipment operation for a set period", "Suspension from duties for 6 months", "Suspension of operation of the station where they work", "Revocation of the radio operator license"], "v": [141, 140, 158, 251, 137, 139, 201, 308, 359, 145, 198, 199, 200, 203, 204, 210, 233, 234, 303, 307, 313, 323, 347, 382]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.3", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no3/", "k": "11", "al": [], "q": "無線局の免許状を１箇月以内に総務大臣に返納しなければならないのはどの場合か。", "x": "", "o": ["無線局の運用を休止したとき。", "無線局の運用の停止を命じられたとき。", "無線局の免許がその効力を失ったとき。", "免許状を破損し、又は汚したとき。"], "a": 2, "e": "<b>免許がその効力を失ったときは、免許人であった者は、一箇月以内にその免許状を返納しなければならない。(電波法 第24条)</b>", "ee": "When a license loses its validity, the former licensee must return the station license within one month. (Radio Act, Art. 24)", "eg": false, "eq": "In which case must a station license be returned to the Minister within 1 month?", "eo": ["When station operation is suspended.", "When ordered to suspend station operation.", "When the station license loses its validity.", "When the license is damaged or soiled."], "v": [158, 139, 147, 145, 152, 155, 203, 207, 210, 275, 303, 313, 318, 325, 343, 353, 423]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.3", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no3/", "k": "12", "al": [], "q": "陸上移動局（包括免許に係る特定無線局を除く。）の免許状は、どこに備え付けておかなければならないか。", "x": "", "o": ["無線設備の常置場所", "基地局の通信室", "基地局の無線設備の設置場所", "免許人の事務所"], "a": 0, "e": "", "ee": "The station license of a land mobile station must be kept at the permanent location (常置場所) of its radio equipment, since the equipment itself moves around. (Radio Act Enforcement Regulations, Art. 38)", "eg": true, "eq": "Where must the license of a land mobile station (excluding specified stations under a comprehensive license) be kept?", "eo": ["The permanent location of the radio equipment", "The communications room of the base station", "The installation location of the base station's equipment", "The licensee's office"], "v": [237, 245, 140, 150, 267, 268, 269, 146, 147, 240, 270, 271, 337, 422]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.2", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no2/", "k": "1", "al": [], "q": "基地局を開設しようとする者は、どうしなければならないか。", "x": "", "o": ["総務大臣の免許を受ける。", "基地局の運用開始の予定期日を総務大臣に届け出る。", "基地局を開設した旨、遅滞なく総務大臣に届け出る。", "主任無線従事者を選任する。"], "a": 0, "e": "<b>無線局(基地局)を開設しようとする者は、総務大臣の免許を受けなければならない。(電波法 第4条)</b>", "ee": "A person who wants to establish a radio station (base station) must obtain a license from the Minister. (Radio Act, Art. 4)", "eg": false, "eq": "What must a person who intends to establish a base station do?", "eo": ["Obtain a license from the Minister.", "Notify the Minister of the scheduled start date of base station operation.", "Notify the Minister without delay that the base station was established.", "Appoint a chief radio operator."], "v": [142, 158, 162, 166, 211, 212, 240, 308, 145, 169, 209, 309, 312]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.2", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no2/", "k": "2", "al": [], "q": "無線局の無線設備の変更の工事の許可を受けた免許人は、総務省令で定める場合を除き、どのような手続をとった後でなければ、許可に係る無線設備を運用してはならないか。", "x": "", "o": ["総務大臣に運用開始の予定期日を届け出た後", "工事が完了した後、その運用について総務大臣の許可を受けた後", "総務大臣の検査を受け、当該工事の結果が許可の内容に適合していると認められた後", "当該工事の結果が許可の内容に適合している旨を総務大臣に届け出た後"], "a": 2, "e": "<b>無線設備の設置場所の変更又は無線設備の変更の工事の許可を受けた免許人は、総務大臣の検査を受け、当該変更又は工事の結果が同条同項の許可の内容に適合していると認められた後でなければ、許可に係る無線設備を運用してはならない。ただし、総務省令で定める場合は、この限りでない。(電波法 第18条)</b>", "ee": "A licensee who received permission to change the installation location or modify the radio equipment may not operate that equipment until it passes the Minister's inspection and the results are recognized as conforming to the permission, except in cases set by MIC ordinance. (Radio Act, Art. 18)", "eg": false, "eq": "A licensee who has received permission to make changes (construction work) to a station's radio equipment may not operate that equipment until after which procedure, except in cases specified by MIC ordinance?", "eo": ["After notifying the Minister of the scheduled start date of operation", "After the work is completed and the Minister grants permission for its operation", "After undergoing the Minister's inspection and the results of the work are recognized as conforming to the permitted content", "After notifying the Minister that the results of the work conform to the permitted content"], "v": [140, 158, 159, 211, 212, 139, 146, 162, 323, 161, 172, 175, 176, 177, 178, 210, 302, 308, 318, 337, 377, 378, 399, 422, 446, 312, 324]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.2", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no2/", "k": "3", "al": [{"s": "過去問 令和3年10月", "k": "3", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_question_hoki_0310/"}], "q": "次の記述は、電波の質について述べたものである。電波法の規定に照らし、（　　　）内に入れるべき字句を下の番号から選べ。<br>\n送信設備に使用する電波の（　　　）電波の質は、総務省令で定めるところに適合するものでなければならない。", "x": "", "o": ["周波数の偏差、空中線電力の偏差等", "周波数の偏差及び幅、高調波の強度等", "周波数の偏差及び安定度等", "周波数の偏差及び幅、空中線電力の偏差等"], "a": 1, "e": "<b>電波の質とは、「周波数の偏差」、「周波数の幅」、「高調波の強度」と定義されています。(電波法 第28条)</b>", "ee": "The quality of radio waves is defined as the frequency deviation, the frequency bandwidth, and the harmonic intensity. (Radio Act, Art. 28)", "eg": false, "eq": "The following concerns the quality of radio waves. Under the Radio Act, choose what fills the blank. The quality of radio waves used by transmitting equipment, such as [ ], must conform to MIC ordinance.", "eo": ["frequency deviation, antenna power deviation, etc.", "frequency deviation and bandwidth, harmonic intensity, etc.", "frequency deviation and stability, etc.", "frequency deviation and bandwidth, antenna power deviation, etc."], "v": [186, 159, 179, 401, 42, 113, 137, 181, 315, 323, 356, 138, 160, 178, 180, 182, 305, 306, 310, 316, 319, 320, 321, 304, 314, 317, 326, 357]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.2", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no2/", "k": "4", "al": [], "q": "総務大臣が無線従事者の免許を与えないことができる者は、無線従事者の免許を取り消され、取消しの日からどれほどの期間を経過しないものか。", "x": "", "o": ["６箇月", "１年", "１年６箇月", "２年"], "a": 3, "e": "<b><br>次の各号のいずれかに該当する者に対しては、無線従事者の免許を与えないことができる。\n      <br>・電波法の罪を犯し罰金以上の刑に処せられ、その執行が終わり、又はその執行を受けることがなくなった日から二年を経過しない者\n      <br>・無線従事者の免許を取り消され、取消しの日から二年を経過しない者\n      <br>・著しく心身に欠陥があって無線従事者たるに適しない者</b>", "ee": "The Minister may refuse a radio operator license to:<br>• A person who committed a Radio Act crime and was sentenced to a fine or heavier, until 2 years have passed since the sentence was completed or ceased to apply<br>• A person whose radio operator license was revoked, until 2 years have passed since the revocation<br>• A person with a serious mental or physical impairment making them unfit to be a radio operator", "eg": false, "eq": "The Minister may refuse to grant a radio operator license to a person whose license was revoked, if how long has not yet passed since the revocation?", "eo": ["6 months", "1 year", "1 year 6 months", "2 years"], "v": [141, 158, 202, 201, 145, 222, 303, 344, 347, 309, 311, 535]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.2", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no2/", "k": "5", "al": [], "q": "第三級陸上特殊無線技士の資格を有する者が、陸上の無線局の空中線電力５０ワット以下の無線設備（レーダー及び人工衛星局の中継により無線通信を行う無線局の多重無線設備を除く。）の外部の転換装置で電波の質に影響を及ぼさないものの技術操作を行うことができる周波数の電波はどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["２５,０１０ｋＨｚから９６０ＭＨｚまで", "１,６０６.５ｋＨｚから４,０００ｋＨｚまで", "４,０００ｋＨｚから２５,０１０ｋＨｚまで", "９６０ＭＨｚから１,２１５ＭＨｚまで"], "a": 0, "e": "<b>第三級陸上特殊無線技士の技術操作範囲は、下記の通りです。<br>\n      固定局、基地局等の陸上の無線局（注１）の無線設備（レーダー及び人工衛星局の中継により無線通信を行う無線局の多重無線設備を除く。）で次のもの<br>\n      － ５０Ｗ以下の無線設備で２５，０１０ｋＨｚ～９６０ＭＨｚまでの周波数の電波を使用するもの<br>\n      － １００Ｗ以下の無線設備で１，２１５ＭＨｚ以上の周波数の電波を使用するもの<br>\n      (注１)陸上の無線局とは、海岸局、海岸地球局、船舶局、船舶地球局、航空局、航空地球局、航空機局、航空機地球局、無線航行局及び基幹放送局<span>以外</span>の無線局をいう。</b><br>\n      <br>\n      <br><b>技術操作の操作範囲は下記の通りになります。(日本無線協会の資料引用)</b>\n      <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/8230859a63.png\" \n          alt=\"技術操作の操作範囲\"  >\n      </div>", "ee": "The technical operation scope of a 3rd Class Land Special Radio Operator covers equipment of land stations (note 1) such as fixed and base stations (excluding radar and multiplex equipment of stations relaying via satellite):<br>– Equipment of 50 W or less using 25,010 kHz to 960 MHz<br>– Equipment of 100 W or less using 1,215 MHz or higher<br>(Note 1) \"Land stations\" means stations other than coast, coast earth, ship, ship earth, aeronautical, aeronautical earth, aircraft, aircraft earth, radionavigation and core broadcasting stations.<br>Operation scope chart (from the Japan Radio Association): <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/8230859a63.png\" \n          alt=\"技術操作の操作範囲\"  >\n      </div>", "eg": false, "eq": "For a person holding the 3rd Class Land Special Radio Operator qualification, on which frequency range may they perform technical operation of external switching devices that do not affect radio wave quality, on land-station equipment with antenna power of 50 W or less (excluding radar and multiplex equipment of stations relaying via satellite)?", "eo": ["25,010 kHz to 960 MHz", "1,606.5 kHz to 4,000 kHz", "4,000 kHz to 25,010 kHz", "960 MHz to 1,215 MHz"], "v": [144, 247, 186, 244, 140, 143, 179, 248, 249, 42, 139, 338, 536, 138, 227, 236, 246, 307, 310, 328, 337, 342, 402, 309]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.2", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no2/", "k": "6", "al": [], "q": "無線従事者がその免許証の再交付を受けることができる場合に該当しないものはどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["氏名に変更を生じたとき。", "住所に変更を生じたとき。", "免許証を汚したとき。", "免許証を失ったとき。"], "a": 1, "e": "<b>住所を変更しても免許証の再交付は不要です。<br>\n      免許証には下記の内容が記載されます。免許証には、「免許証の番号」、「免許の年月日(免許取得日)」、「氏名」、「生年月日」が記載されていますが、住所は記載されていません。</b>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/ce7720359a.png\" \n          alt=\"無線従事者免許証\"  >\n      </div>", "ee": "A change of address does not require reissuing the license card. The card shows the license number, date of license, name and date of birth, but not the address.<div><img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/ce7720359a.png\" \n          alt=\"無線従事者免許証\"  ></div>", "eg": false, "eq": "Which is NOT a case in which a radio operator can get their license card reissued?", "eo": ["When their name changes.", "When their address changes.", "When the license card is soiled.", "When they lose their license card."], "v": [141, 148, 151, 308, 175, 278, 279, 318, 325, 354, 360, 423]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.2", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no2/", "k": "7", "al": [], "q": "次の記述は、秘密の保護について述べたものである。電波法の規定に照らし、（　　　）内に入れるべき字句を下の番号から選べ。<br><br>\n何人も法律に別段の定めがある場合を除くほか、（　　　）を傍受してその存在若しくは内容を漏らし、又はこれを窃用してはならない。", "x": "", "o": ["総務省令で定める周波数を使用して行われる無線通信", "総務省令で定める周波数を使用して行われる暗語による無線通信", "特定の相手方に対して行われる無線通信", "特定の相手方に対して行われる暗語による無線通信"], "a": 2, "e": "<b>何人も法律に別段の定めがある場合を除くほか、特定の相手方に対して行われる無線通信を傍受してその存在若しくは内容を漏らし、又はこれを窃用してはならない。</b>", "ee": "Unless otherwise provided by law, no person shall intercept radio communications addressed to a specific party and disclose their existence or content, or make illicit use of them.", "eg": false, "eq": "The following concerns protection of secrecy. Under the Radio Act, choose what fills the blank. Unless otherwise provided by law, no person shall intercept ( ) and disclose its existence or content, or make illicit use of it.", "eo": ["radio communications using frequencies specified by MIC ordinance", "radio communications in code using frequencies specified by MIC ordinance", "radio communications addressed to a specific party", "radio communications in code addressed to a specific party"], "v": [286, 292, 143, 159, 527, 42, 137, 261, 289, 291, 315, 323, 356, 380, 160, 287, 288, 290, 305, 306, 307, 313, 316, 318, 319, 320, 321, 337, 377, 447, 475, 526, 304, 314, 317]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.2", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no2/", "k": "8", "al": [], "q": "無線局の臨時検査（電波法第７３条第５項の検査）において検査されることがあるものはどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["無線従事者の資格及び員数", "無線従事者の業務経歴", "無線従事者の勤務状況", "無線従事者の知識及び技能"], "a": 0, "e": "<b>無線局の臨時検査（電波法第７３条第５項の検査）において検査されることがあるものは、無線従事者の資格及び員数(人数, 人員の数)になります。</b>", "ee": "What may be inspected in an extraordinary inspection (Radio Act Art. 73, Para. 5) is the radio operators' qualifications and number (headcount).", "eg": false, "eq": "What may be inspected in an extraordinary inspection of a station (Radio Act Art. 73, Para. 5)?", "eo": ["The radio operators' qualifications and number", "The radio operators' work history", "The radio operators' work status", "The radio operators' knowledge and skills"], "v": [141, 173, 231, 232, 137, 139, 172, 227, 228, 229, 230, 310, 406, 407, 408]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.2", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no2/", "k": "9", "al": [], "q": "総務大臣から無線局の免許が取り消されることがあるのはどの場合か。", "x": "", "o": ["免許状を失ったとき。", "運用許容時間外の運用をしたとき。", "免許状に記載されていない周波数の電波を使用したとき。", "不正な手段により無線局の免許を受けたとき。"], "a": 3, "e": "<b>無線局の免許が取り消されることがあるのは、不正な手段により無線局の免許を受けたときになります。</b>", "ee": "A station license may be revoked when it was obtained by fraudulent means.", "eg": false, "eq": "In which case may the Minister revoke a station license?", "eo": ["When the station license is lost.", "When operating outside the permitted operating hours.", "When using a frequency not stated on the station license.", "When the station license was obtained by fraudulent means."], "v": [213, 224, 158, 202, 42, 139, 147, 138, 145, 210, 308, 318, 320, 325, 348, 473]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.2", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no2/", "k": "10", "al": [], "q": "総務大臣から無線従事者がその免許を取り消されることがあるのはどの場合か。", "x": "", "o": ["免許証を失ったとき。", "引き続き５年以上無線設備の操作を行わなかったとき。", "日本の国籍を有しない者となったとき。", "電波法に違反したとき。"], "a": 3, "e": "<b>電波法に違反した場合、無線従事者免許を取り消されることがあります。</b>", "ee": "A radio operator license may be revoked for violating the Radio Act.", "eg": false, "eq": "In which case may the Minister revoke a radio operator's license?", "eo": ["When they lose their license card.", "When they have not operated radio equipment for 5 consecutive years or more.", "When they no longer hold Japanese nationality.", "When they violate the Radio Act."], "v": [141, 140, 158, 202, 405, 137, 148, 145, 199, 223, 250, 307, 318, 325, 338, 341, 358, 309, 535]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.2", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no2/", "k": "11", "al": [], "q": "無線局の免許がその効力を失ったときは、免許人であった者は、その免許状をどうしなければならない\nか。", "x": "", "o": ["２年間保管する。", "１箇月以内に総務大臣に返納する。", "３箇月以内に総務大臣に返納する。", "直ちに廃棄する。"], "a": 1, "e": "<b>無線局の免許がその効力を失ったときは、免許人であった者は、１箇月以内に総務大臣に返納する必要があります。</b>", "ee": "When a station license loses its validity, the former licensee must return it to the Minister within 1 month.", "eg": false, "eq": "When a station license loses its validity, what must the former licensee do with the license document?", "eo": ["Keep it for 2 years.", "Return it to the Minister within 1 month.", "Return it to the Minister within 3 months.", "Destroy it immediately."], "v": [158, 139, 146, 147, 168, 145, 152, 155, 273, 276, 303, 325, 343, 452, 309]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.2", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no2/", "k": "12", "al": [], "q": "基地局に備え付けておかなければならない書類はどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["免許状", "無線従事者選解任届の写し", "無線設備等の点検実施報告書の写し", "免許証"], "a": 0, "e": "<b>基地局には免許状を備え付けておく必要があります。</b>", "ee": "The station license must be kept at the base station.", "eg": false, "eq": "Which document must be kept at a base station?", "eo": ["Station license (免許状)", "Copy of the radio operator appointment/dismissal notice", "Copy of the radio equipment inspection report", "Operator license card (免許証)"], "v": [141, 140, 171, 267, 147, 148, 240, 529, 264, 265, 266, 528, 326]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.1", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no1/", "k": "1", "al": [], "q": "「無線局」の定義として、正しいものはどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["無線設備及び無線設備の操作を行う者の総体をいう。ただし、受信のみを目的とするものを含まない。", "無線設備及び無線従事者の総体をいう。ただし、発射する電波が著しく微弱で総務省令で定めるものを含まない。", "無線設備及び無線設備の操作の監督を行う者の総体をいう。", "無線設備及び無線設備を管理する者の総体をいう。"], "a": 0, "e": "<b>無線局とは「無線設備及び無線設備の操作を行う者の総体」を意味します。\n      <br>ただし、受信専用のものは含みません。(電波法 第2条)</b>", "ee": "A radio station means \"the whole of radio equipment and the persons who operate it,\" excluding stations intended only for reception. (Radio Act, Art. 2)", "eg": false, "eq": "Which is the correct definition of \"radio station\" (無線局)?", "eo": ["The whole of radio equipment and the persons who operate it; excluding those intended only for reception.", "The whole of radio equipment and radio operators; excluding those whose emissions are extremely weak as specified by MIC ordinance.", "The whole of radio equipment and the persons who supervise its operation.", "The whole of radio equipment and the persons who manage it."], "v": [141, 140, 159, 139, 257, 322, 323, 131, 138, 250, 252, 253, 254, 255, 256, 280, 307, 310, 410, 425, 309]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.1", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no1/", "k": "2", "al": [], "q": "無線局の免許人があらかじめ総務大臣の許可を受けなければならないのはどの場合か。", "x": "", "o": ["無線局の運用を休止しようとするとき。", "無線局の運用を開始しようとするとき。", "無線設備の設置場所を変更しようとするとき。", "無線局を廃止しようとするとき。"], "a": 2, "e": "<b>無線設備の設置場所変更：総務大臣の許可が必要になります。(電波法 第17条)</b>\n      <br>運用開始：無線局の開局のために免許は必要ですが、運用開始のための許可は不要です。\n      <br>運用休止：総務大臣の許可は不要です。\n      <br>運用廃止：運用を廃止する際は届出が必要になりますが、総務大臣の許可は不要です。", "ee": "Changing the installation location: requires the Minister's permission. (Radio Act, Art. 17)<br>Starting operation: a license is needed to open a station, but no permission is needed to start operating.<br>Suspending operation: no permission from the Minister is needed.<br>Closing the station: a notification is required, but not the Minister's permission.", "eg": false, "eq": "In which case must a station licensee obtain the Minister's permission in advance?", "eo": ["When intending to suspend station operation.", "When intending to start station operation.", "When intending to change the installation location of the radio equipment.", "When intending to close the station."], "v": [140, 158, 269, 139, 146, 161, 175, 207, 208, 210, 308, 318, 530]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.1", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no1/", "k": "3", "al": [], "q": "次の記述は、電波の質について述べたものである。電波法の規定に照らし、（　　　）内に入れるべき字句を下の番号から選べ。<br>\n送信設備に使用する電波の（　　　）、高調波の強度等電波の質は、総務省令で定めるところに適合するものでなければならない。", "x": "", "o": ["空中線電力の偏差", "周波数の偏差及び幅", "周波数の安定度", "変調度"], "a": 1, "e": "<b>電波の質とは、「周波数の偏差」、「周波数の幅」、「高調波の強度」と定義されています。(電波法 第28条)</b>", "ee": "The quality of radio waves is defined as the frequency deviation, the frequency bandwidth, and the harmonic intensity. (Radio Act, Art. 28)", "eg": false, "eq": "The following concerns the quality of radio waves. Under the Radio Act, choose what fills the blank. The quality of radio waves used by transmitting equipment, such as ( ), harmonic intensity, etc., must conform to MIC ordinance.", "eo": ["antenna power deviation", "frequency deviation and bandwidth", "frequency stability", "modulation depth"], "v": [186, 159, 179, 401, 42, 113, 137, 181, 183, 315, 323, 356, 138, 160, 178, 180, 182, 305, 306, 310, 316, 319, 320, 321, 304, 314, 317, 326, 357]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.1", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no1/", "k": "4", "al": [], "q": "次の記述は、「無線従事者」の定義である。電波法の規定に照らし、（　　　）内に入れるべき字句を下の番号から選べ。<br>\n「無線従事者」とは、（　　　）であって、総務大臣の免許を受けたものをいう。", "x": "", "o": ["無線設備の操作又はその監督を行う者", "無線局に配置された者", "無線局を運用する者", "無線局を管理する者"], "a": 0, "e": "<b>無線従事者とは、「無線設備の操作又はその監督を行う者」と定義されています。(電波法 第2条)</b>", "ee": "A radio operator is defined as \"a person who operates radio equipment or supervises its operation.\" (Radio Act, Art. 2)", "eg": false, "eq": "The following is the definition of \"radio operator.\" Under the Radio Act, choose what fills the blank. A \"radio operator\" means ( ) who has received a license from the Minister.", "eo": ["a person who operates radio equipment or supervises its operation", "a person assigned to a radio station", "a person who operates a radio station", "a person who manages a radio station"], "v": [141, 140, 158, 137, 139, 315, 356, 145, 160, 210, 250, 252, 253, 254, 305, 306, 307, 308, 313, 316, 319, 449, 304, 309, 314, 317]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.1", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no1/", "k": "5", "al": [], "q": "第三級陸上特殊無線技士の資格を有する者が、陸上の無線局の１,２１５ＭＨｚ以上の周波数の電波を使用する無線設備（レーダー及び人工衛星局の中継により無線通信を行う無線局の多重無線設備を除く。）の外部の転換装置で電波の質に影響を及ぼさないものの技術操作を行うことができるのは、空中線電力何ワット以下のものか。", "x": "", "o": ["２５ワット", "１０ワット", "２５０ワット", "１００ワット"], "a": 3, "e": "<b>第三級陸上特殊無線技士の技術操作範囲は、下記の通りです。<br>\n      固定局、基地局等の陸上の無線局（注１）の無線設備（レーダー及び人工衛星局の中継により無線通信を行う無線局の多重無線設備を除く。）で次のもの<br>\n      － ５０Ｗ以下の無線設備で２５，０１０ｋＨｚ～９６０ＭＨｚまでの周波数の電波を使用するもの<br>\n      － １００Ｗ以下の無線設備で１，２１５ＭＨｚ以上の周波数の電波を使用するもの<br>\n      (注１)陸上の無線局とは、海岸局、海岸地球局、船舶局、船舶地球局、航空局、航空地球局、航空機局、航空機地球局、無線航行局及び基幹放送局<span>以外</span>の無線局をいう。</b><br>\n      <br>\n      技術操作の操作範囲は下記の通りになります。(日本無線協会の資料引用)\n      <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/8230859a63.png\" \n          alt=\"技術操作の操作範囲\"  >\n      </div>", "ee": "The technical operation scope of a 3rd Class Land Special Radio Operator covers equipment of land stations (note 1) such as fixed and base stations (excluding radar and multiplex equipment of stations relaying via satellite):<br>– Equipment of 50 W or less using 25,010 kHz to 960 MHz<br>– Equipment of 100 W or less using 1,215 MHz or higher<br>(Note 1) \"Land stations\" means stations other than coast, coast earth, ship, ship earth, aeronautical, aeronautical earth, aircraft, aircraft earth, radionavigation and core broadcasting stations.<br>Operation scope chart (from the Japan Radio Association): <div>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" \n          src=\"img/8230859a63.png\" \n          alt=\"技術操作の操作範囲\"  >\n      </div>", "eg": false, "eq": "A 3rd Class Land Special Radio Operator may perform technical operation of external switching devices that do not affect wave quality, on land-station equipment using frequencies of 1,215 MHz or higher (excluding radar and multiplex equipment relaying via satellite), up to what antenna power?", "eo": ["25 W", "10 W", "250 W", "100 W"], "v": [144, 247, 186, 244, 140, 143, 179, 248, 249, 542, 42, 139, 338, 536, 138, 227, 236, 246, 307, 310, 320, 328, 337, 341, 342, 402, 309]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.1", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no1/", "k": "6", "al": [], "q": "無線従事者は、その業務に従事しているときは、免許証をどのようにしていなければならないか。", "x": "", "o": ["通信室内に保管する。", "携帯する。", "通信室内の見やすい箇所に掲げる。", "無線局に備え付ける。"], "a": 1, "e": "<b>無線局の運用時は、無線従事者免許証を携帯している必要があります。</b>", "ee": "While operating a radio station, the operator must carry their radio operator license card.", "eg": false, "eq": "While engaged in their duties, how must a radio operator keep their license card?", "eo": ["Store it in the communications room.", "Carry it on their person.", "Post it in a visible place in the communications room.", "Keep it at the radio station."], "v": [141, 267, 531, 139, 148, 270, 533, 233, 234, 272, 273, 532, 314]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.1", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no1/", "k": "7", "al": [], "q": "無線局がなるべく擬似空中線回路を使用しなければならないのはどの場合か。", "x": "", "o": ["他の無線局の通信に混信を与えるおそれがあるとき。", "工事設計書に記載した空中線を使用できないとき。", "総務大臣の行う無線局の検査のために運用するとき。", "無線設備の機器の試験又は調整を行うために運用するとき。"], "a": 3, "e": "<b>疑似空中線とはダミーロードとも呼ばれており、無線設備の機器の試験又は調整を行う際に使用して、電波を送信しなくても試験/調整をするためものです。</b>", "ee": "A dummy antenna (also called a dummy load) is used when testing or adjusting radio equipment, so tests and adjustments can be done without actually radiating radio waves.", "eg": false, "eq": "In which case should a station use a dummy antenna circuit as much as possible?", "eo": ["When there is a risk of causing interference to other stations' communications.", "When the antenna listed in the construction design document cannot be used.", "When operating for a station inspection conducted by the Minister.", "When operating to test or adjust radio equipment."], "v": [187, 263, 140, 158, 139, 185, 344, 63, 108, 172, 210, 307, 313, 318, 320, 348, 349, 404, 451, 450]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.1", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no1/", "k": "8", "al": [], "q": "総務大臣は、無線局の発射する電波の質が総務省令で定めるものに適合していないと認めるときは、その無線局に対してどのような処分を行うことができるか。", "x": "", "o": ["無線局の免許を取り消す。", "空中線の撤去を命ずる。", "周波数又は空中線電力の指定を変更する。", "臨時に電波の発射の停止を命ずる。"], "a": 3, "e": "<b>電波の質が適合していないと臨時に電波の発射の停止を命じられます。</b>", "ee": "If the quality of radio waves does not conform, the station can be ordered to temporarily stop emitting radio waves.", "eg": false, "eq": "When the Minister finds that the quality of radio waves emitted by a station does not conform to MIC ordinance, what action can the Minister take against that station?", "eo": ["Revoke the station license.", "Order removal of the antenna.", "Change the designated frequency or antenna power.", "Temporarily order the station to stop emitting radio waves."], "v": [186, 158, 159, 179, 202, 42, 139, 185, 323, 353, 378, 380, 131, 138, 145, 174, 175, 178, 197, 198, 203, 206, 307, 313]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.1", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no1/", "k": "9", "al": [], "q": "無線局の免許人が電波法又は電波法に基づく命令に違反したときに総務大臣が行うことができる処分はどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["無線局の運用の停止", "再免許の拒否", "通信の相手方又は通信事項の制限", "電波の型式の制限"], "a": 0, "e": "<b>無線局の免許人が、電波法又は電波法に基づく命令に違反したときは無線局の運用の停止が命じられます。</b>", "ee": "When a licensee violates the Radio Act or orders based on it, suspension of station operation can be ordered.", "eg": false, "eq": "What action can the Minister take when a station licensee violates the Radio Act or orders based on it?", "eo": ["Suspension of station operation", "Refusal of license renewal", "Restriction of communication counterparts or communication matters", "Restriction of emission type"], "v": [158, 260, 137, 139, 146, 149, 261, 359, 138, 188, 198, 199, 200, 203, 204, 205, 210, 307, 313, 349]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.1", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no1/", "k": "10", "al": [], "q": "総務大臣から無線従事者がその免許を取り消されることがある場合に該当しないものはどれか。", "x": "", "o": ["電波法若しくは電波法に基づく命令又はこれらに基づく処分に違反したとき。", "著しく心身に欠陥があって無線従事者たるに適しない者に該当するに至ったとき。", "引き続き５年以上無線設備の操作を行わなかったとき。", "不正な手段により無線従事者の免許を受けたとき。"], "a": 2, "e": "<b>５年以上無線設備の操作を行わなくても、無線従事者免許が取り消される事はありません。</b>", "ee": "A radio operator license is not revoked just because the holder has not operated radio equipment for 5 years or more.", "eg": false, "eq": "Which is NOT a case in which the Minister may revoke a radio operator's license?", "eo": ["When they violate the Radio Act, orders based on it, or dispositions based on those.", "When they come to have a serious mental or physical impairment making them unfit to be a radio operator.", "When they have not operated radio equipment for 5 consecutive years or more.", "When they obtained the radio operator license by fraudulent means."], "v": [141, 224, 140, 158, 202, 405, 527, 137, 257, 359, 145, 198, 199, 200, 225, 226, 250, 307, 308, 313, 318, 341, 354, 474, 534, 309, 535]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.1", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no1/", "k": "11", "al": [], "q": "無線局の免許人は、免許状に記載した事項に変更を生じたときは、どうしなければならないか。", "x": "", "o": ["免許状を総務大臣に提出し、訂正を受ける。", "総務大臣に免許状の再交付を申請する。", "遅滞なく、その旨を総務大臣に報告する。", "直ちに、その旨を総務大臣に届け出る。"], "a": 0, "e": "<b>免許状に記載した事項に変更があった場合、免許状を総務大臣に提出し、訂正を受ける必要があります。</b>", "ee": "When a matter stated on the station license changes, the license must be submitted to the Minister for correction.", "eg": false, "eq": "What must a station licensee do when a matter stated on the station license changes?", "eo": ["Submit the license to the Minister and have it corrected.", "Apply to the Minister for reissue of the license.", "Report to the Minister without delay.", "Notify the Minister immediately."], "v": [158, 162, 166, 139, 146, 147, 151, 168, 308, 156, 163, 175, 296, 348, 360, 381, 409, 312]}, {"c": "law", "s": "例題集 No.1", "u": "https://funfun-wireless-communication.com/3riku_hoki_exercise_no1/", "k": "12", "al": [], "q": "無線局の免許人は、無線従事者を選任し、又は解任したときは、どうしなければならないか。", "x": "", "o": ["１箇月以内にその旨を総務大臣に報告する。", "遅滞なく、その旨を総務大臣に届け出る。", "２週間以内にその旨を総務大臣に届け出る。", "速やかに総務大臣の承認を受ける。"], "a": 1, "e": "<b>無線従事者を選任し、又は解任したときは、遅滞なく、その旨を総務大臣に届け出る必要があります。</b>", "ee": "When a radio operator is appointed or dismissed, the Minister must be notified without delay.", "eg": false, "eq": "When a licensee appoints or dismisses a radio operator, what must they do?", "eo": ["Report to the Minister within 1 month.", "Notify the Minister without delay.", "Notify the Minister within 2 weeks.", "Promptly obtain the Minister's approval."], "v": [141, 158, 162, 166, 167, 139, 146, 308, 163, 164, 169, 170, 303, 313, 343, 403, 312]}];
